window.ZIKRA_CONTENT=window.ZIKRA_CONTENT||{};window.ZIKRA_CONTENT.en=[{"id":2,"text":"There is none worthy of worship except Allah alone with no partner or associate. He is the Dominion and to Him be all praise, and He is able to do all things. O Allah, one can withhold what You have given and none can give what You have withheld, and no wealth or fortune can benefit anyone for from You comes all wealth and fortune.","title":"Dua After Prayer for Rizq and Help","source":"Bukhari: 844","reflection":"This dua after salah reminds us that only Allah controls all wealth and blessings, making it a strong way to ask for rizq and help after every fard prayer in daily life.","lesson":"Allahumma la mania lima ataita brings Barakah in rizq and keeps wealth safe."},{"id":3,"text":"None has the right to be worshipped but Allah alone, Who has no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is Able to do all things.","title":"Power of La Ilaha Illallah (Freeing of slave)","source":"Bukhari: 6404","reflection":"Saying the kalima tawhid brings a muslim closer to Allah’s mercy and power, making hearts strong and filling life with blessings through this most powerful dua in Islam.","lesson":"Kalima tawhid wipes away many sins and brings Barakah in every Amal and day."},{"id":4,"text":"It is You we worship and It is You we ask for help.","title":"Dua for Guidance (Recitation of Surah Al-Fatiha)","source":"Surah Al-Fatihah 1:5","reflection":"This dua for guidance from Surah Al Fatihah helps muslims ask Allah for help and direction, making every Salah and Amal full of hope and trust in His mercy and wisdom.","lesson":"Iyyaka na budu wa iyyaka nastaeen brings true guidance in every muslim’s life."},{"id":5,"text":"Guide me through that which there has been difference concerning the truth, verily, You are upon a straight path.","title":"Prophetic Du'a for Guidance (Sahih Muslim)","source":"Muslim: 770","reflection":"This prophetic dua for guidance from Sahih Muslim helps muslims find the right path when truth is unclear, making hearts steady with Allah’s help and the meaning of tawheed in Islam.","lesson":"Prophetic dua for guidance brings muslims closer to sirat al mustaqim always."},{"id":6,"text":"O Allah, help me to remember You, to give You thanks, and to perform Your worship in the best manner.","title":"Dua after Salah for Help in Worship","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1522","reflection":"This dua after salah helps muslims remember Allah, thank Him, and do ibadah in the best way, making every prayer full of Barakah and true Amal for the heart.","lesson":"Allahumma inni ala zikrika keeps zikr strong and brings peace after every namaz."},{"id":7,"text":"Guide me to the best of manners for none can guide to the best of them but You. Protect me from bad manners for none can protect against them but You.","title":"Dua for Good manners (Masnoon Dua)","source":"Muslim: 771","reflection":"Asking Allah for the best manners brings kindness and respect in life, making every action better and keeping hearts soft with this masnoon dua for good character and daily Amal.","lesson":"Allah guides a muslim to the best akhlaq by this dua for good manner."},{"id":8,"text":"O Allah, I beg of Thee righteousness and adhering to the straight path.","title":"Dua for Guidance","source":"Muslim: 2725","reflection":"Asking Allah for guidance and strength with this powerful dua brings light to the heart, helps a muslim stay on the right path, and keeps Iman strong in every step of daily life.","lesson":"Allahumma inni dua for guidance leads a muslim to the straight path always."},{"id":9,"text":"O Allah, guide me with those whom You have guided, and strengthen me with those whom You have given strength. Take me to Your care with those whom You have taken to Your care. Bless me in what You have given me. Protect me from the evil You have ordained. Surely, You command and are not commanded, and none whom You have committed to Your care shall be humiliated and none whom You have taken as an enemy shall taste glory. You are Blessed, Our Lord, and Exalted.","title":"Powerful Night Prayer in Witr (Dua Qunoot)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1425","reflection":"This powerful night prayer in Witr brings Allah’s help, Barakah, and safety, making hearts strong and keeping a muslim close to Allah’s care every night in Salah.","lesson":"Dua qunoot in witr prayer brings Allah’s hidayat and keeps Iman strong."},{"id":11,"text":"O Allah forgive me and accept my repentance, for You are the Accepter of repentance, the Most Merciful.","title":"Dua for forgiveness (Rabbighfirli wa tub alayya innaka)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1516","reflection":"Asking Allah for forgiveness with this short dua brings peace to the heart, helps a muslim clean his Amal, and keeps hope alive for Allah’s mercy and kindness every day.","lesson":"Rabbighfirli dua wipes away sins and brings Allah’s Rahmah close to the heart."},{"id":12,"text":"I seek the forgiveness of Allah the Mighty, Whom there is none worthy of worship except Him, the Living, the Eternal, and I repent to Him.","title":"Dua for forgiveness for major sins","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3577","reflection":"Turning to Allah with this dua for forgiveness of major sins brings hope, wipes away big mistakes, and helps a muslim feel Allah’s mercy and Barakah in every part of life.","lesson":"Astaghfirullah al adzim dua removes heavy sins and brings Allah’s maghfirat."},{"id":13,"text":"O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and seek Your protection from the Fire.","title":"Paradise and Hell Fire Dua for protection","source":"Sahih (Albani). Ibn Majah: 910","reflection":"Asking Allah for Jannah and safety from Jahannam with this dua brings hope, keeps hearts focused on the hereafter, and helps a Muslim remember the real goal of life every day.","lesson":"Allahumma inni asaluka makes a Muslim’s wish for Jannah strong in every Salah."},{"id":15,"text":"O Allah! Controller of the hearts, direct our hearts to Your obedience.","title":"Dua for Hearts to obedience (Sahih Muslim)","source":"Muslim: 2655","reflection":"Asking Allah to guide the heart with this dua brings calm, helps a Muslim stay on the right path, and keeps the heart close to Allah’s commands in every part of life.","lesson":"Ya muqollibal qulub helps hearts stay soft and ready for Allah’s Hidayat."},{"id":16,"text":"O Changer of the Hearts! Strengthen my heart upon Your Religion.","title":"Dua For Steadfast In Religion (Masnun Dua)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3522","reflection":"Asking Allah to keep the heart strong on His Deen with this dua helps a Muslim stay firm, brings peace, and keeps Iman safe from doubts and wrong ways every single day.","lesson":"Ya muqallibal qulub dua in Arabic keeps the heart steady on true Islam."},{"id":17,"text":"O Allah! grant us a good outcome on all of our affairs and save us from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter.","title":"Dua for Protection in all activities (Masnoon Dua)","source":"Sahih (Suyuti). Jami'us Sagir: 1450","reflection":"Asking Allah for a good end in every matter with this dua brings safety, keeps a Muslim away from shame, and helps the heart trust Allah’s plan in both this world and the next.","lesson":"Allahumma dua for protection keeps a Muslim safe from all kinds of evil."},{"id":18,"text":"O Allah perfect for me my religion on which success of all my affairs depends, And perfect my worldly affairs on which my livelihood depends, And perfect my hereafter to which I will return, And make in life for me an increase of all good, And make death for me a comfort from all evil.","title":"Dua for success in Deen (Allahumma aslih li deeni)","source":"Muslim: 2720","reflection":"Asking Allah with this dua for success brings help in Deen, Dunya, and Akhirah, keeps a Muslim’s life full of Barakah, and makes every day better with Allah’s mercy and care.","lesson":"Allahumma aslih li deeni helps keep Deen strong and Amal safe from mistakes."},{"id":19,"text":"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from deprivation of Your blessing, alteration of Your protection, sudden infliction of Your anger, and all Your wrath.","title":"Dua for Protection and seek Allah's help","source":"Muslim: 2739","reflection":"This dua of protection asks Allah to keep His blessings safe, protect from harm, and help every Muslim stay strong in times of trouble and fear.","lesson":"Allah gives His Barakah and keeps blessings safe when this dua for protection is made."},{"id":20,"text":"O Allah, I seek refuge in you from grief and sadness, from weakness and from laziness, from miserliness and from cowardice, from being overcome by debt and overpowered by men (i.e. others).","title":"Dua for Stress, Anxiety and Depression","source":"Bukhari :2893","reflection":"This dua for stress and sadness helps a Muslim find peace, strength, and relief from heavy feelings, asking Allah to remove worries, debt, and all kinds of hardship from life.","lesson":"Allah removes sadness and gives peace when this dua for stress is made with Iman."},{"id":22,"text":"Glorified is Allah and praised is He.","title":"Dua for Forgiveness of Sins","source":"Bukhari: 6405","reflection":"This dua for forgiveness of sins brings Allah’s mercy, wipes away mistakes, and fills the heart with Barakah and peace for every Muslim who says it with Iman.","lesson":"Allah forgives many sins when a Muslim says subhanallahi wa bihamdihi."},{"id":23,"text":"Glory be to Allah and all praise is due to him, glory be to Allah the great.","title":"Dhikr for Forgiveness (Subhanallah Wa Bihamdihi Dua)","source":"Bukhari: 6406","reflection":"This dhikr and dua brings Allah’s forgiveness, fills the heart with Barakah, and makes every Muslim’s Amal shine with the blessings of praising Allah’s greatness and mercy.","lesson":"Allah forgives many sins when a Muslim says subhanallahi wa bihamdihi subhanallahil azeem."},{"id":24,"text":"How perfect Allah is, and all praise is for Allah. None has the right to be worshipped except Allah, and Allah is the greatest. [1]","title":"Powerful Dhikr Beloved to Allah (Masnun Dua)","source":"[1] Muslim: 2137 [2] Muslim: 2695","reflection":"This powerful zikr brings hearts closer to Allah and fills life with Barakah, as these words are loved by Allah and easy for every Muslim to say in any moment.","lesson":"Subhanallah walhamdulillah wala ilaha illallah wallahu akbar brings huge reward from Allah and makes Iman strong."},{"id":25,"text":"How perfect Allah is.","title":"Benefits of Saying Subhan Allah","source":"Muslim: 2698","reflection":"Saying SubhanAllah brings a Muslim closer to Allah’s love and forgiveness, making hearts clean and filling every evening with peace and blessings from the best dhikr.","lesson":"SubhanAllah in arabic removes small sins and brings Barakah in Amal."},{"id":26,"text":"In the name of Allah, the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful. (1) Say, \"He is Allah, [who is] One, (2) Allah, the Eternal Refuge. (3) He neither begets nor is born, (4) Nor is there to Him any equivalent.\" (Sura Ikhlas: 1-4)","title":"Benefits of Surah Ikhlas Daily Recitation","source":"Sahih (Albani). Sahih Al Jame: 6472","reflection":"Surah Ikhlas brings huge reward and makes Iman strong, as this short surah is equal to one third of the Quran and fills the heart with love for Allah every day.","lesson":"Surah Ikhlas in Arabic gives reward like reading one third of Quran."},{"id":27,"text":"How perfect Allah is, The Supreme, and I praise Him.","title":"Daily dua for planting a tree in Jannah","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3464","reflection":"This dua for Jannah helps a Muslim earn trees in Paradise and brings Allah’s praise and mercy closer, making every day full of hope and reward for the hereafter.","lesson":"Subhanallahi wa bihamdihi subhanallahil azeem plants a tree in Jannah."},{"id":28,"text":"There is no might nor power except with Allah.","title":"Dua for Jannah (Lahaula Walaquwata)","source":"Bukhari: 6384","reflection":"This jannat dua reminds every Muslim that all strength comes from Allah alone, bringing hope, reward, and help in every hard time for those who trust in His power.","lesson":"La hawla wala quwwata illa billah in arabic opens doors to Jannah for muslims."},{"id":29,"text":"None has the right to be worshipped except Allah, alone without any partener. Allah is most great and much praise is for Allah. How perfect Allah is, Lord of the worlds. There is no might nor power except with Allah, The Exalted in might, The Wise.","title":"Dua of all praise for Allah (Masnoon Dua)","source":"Muslim: 2696","reflection":"This dua praising Allah brings a muslim closer to Him, filling the heart with thankfulness and reminding us of Allah’s greatness, mercy, and power in every part of daily life.","lesson":"Allah’s help comes to the one who says la ilaha illalahu with full Iman."},{"id":30,"text":"O Allah, forgive me, have mercy upon me, guide me and grant me sustenance.","title":"Dua after Accepting Islam (Masnun Dua)","source":"Muslim: 2697","reflection":"This dua after accepting Islam helps a new muslim ask Allah for forgiveness, mercy, guidance, safety, and rizq, making the start of their Iman journey full of hope and Barakah.","lesson":"Allahummaghfirli warhamni brings Allah’s forgiveness and covers old sins."},{"id":31,"text":"All praise is for Allah.","title":"Most Powerful Dhikr and Dua in Islam","source":"Hasan (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3383","reflection":"Saying Alhamdulillah fills the heart with shukr, brings peace, and keeps a muslim close to Allah, making every moment full of Barakah and hope in daily life.","lesson":"Alhamdulillah meaning teaches a muslim to thank Allah in every Amal."},{"id":32,"text":"How perfect Allah is, and all praise is for Allah. None has the right to be worshipped except Allah, and Allah is the greatest. There is no might nor power except with Allah.","title":"Powerful Dhikr That Lasts Forever in Jannah","source":"Musnad-e Ahmad (no. 513) (Ahmad Shakir, ed.) and its chain of narration is authentic. See Majma'uz-Zawa'id 1/297. Ibn Hajar mentions it in Bulughul-Maram saying that Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim considered it authentic.","reflection":"This dhikr and dua fills the heart with Iman, brings Allah’s mercy, and gives rewards that stay forever in Jannah, making every muslim’s Amal strong and full of Barakah.","lesson":"Subhanallah meaning helps a muslim keep the tongue clean with Allah’s zikr."},{"id":36,"text":"(1) Indeed, We sent the Qur'an down during the Night of Decree. (2) And what can make you know what is the Night of Decree? (3) The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months. (4) The angels and the Spirit descend therein by permission of their Lord for every matter. (5) Peace it is until the emergence of dawn.","title":"Benefit of Laylatul Qadr Surah","source":"Surah Al-Qadr 97:1-5","reflection":"Surah al Qadr tells about the Night of Power, bringing huge rewards, peace, and blessings for muslims who read and believe in its message, making every Ramadan night full of hope.","lesson":"Surah al Qadr brings reward better than a thousand months in Amal."},{"id":37,"text":"O Allah, You are Most Forgiving, Generous. You love forgiveness; so forgive me.","title":"Laylatul Qadr dua for forgiveness","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3513","reflection":"On the blessed night of Laylatul Qadr, this dua for forgiveness brings hope and mercy, helping every Muslim seek Allah’s pardon and Barakah in the last 10 days of Ramadan.","lesson":"Allah’s mercy covers the heart of a Muslim who makes laylatul qadr dua."},{"id":39,"text":"(17) They used to sleep but little of the night, (18) And in the hours before dawn they would ask forgiveness. [2]","title":"Dua for Forgiveness at Tahajjud Time","source":"[1] Bukhari: 1145 [2] Surah Az-Zariyat: 51: 17-18","reflection":"","lesson":""},{"id":45,"text":"None has the right to be worshipped but Allah. He is the Only One and has no partners. For Him is the Kingdom and all the praises are due for Him. He is Omnipotent. All the praises are for Allah. All the glories are for Allah. And none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, And Allah is Great And there is neither Might nor Power Except with Allah.","title":"Dua When Waking Up at Night (Masnun Dua)","source":"Bukhari: 1154","reflection":"This dua at night fills the heart with Allah’s praise and power, helping Muslims remember Him after sleep and bringing peace and Barakah in the quiet hours before Fajr.","lesson":"Allah’s help comes close to the one who makes dua when waking up at night."},{"id":46,"text":"There is none worthy of worship but You, glory is to You. Surely, I was among the wrongdoers.","title":"Dua of Yunus (La Ilaha Illa Anta Subhanaka)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3505","reflection":"This dua of Yunus brings hope and relief for Muslims facing mushkil, helping hearts find Allah’s mercy and forgiveness in times of distress and hardship.","lesson":"Allah removes mushkil for the one who calls with dua of yunus in hard times."},{"id":47,"text":"We are from Allah and unto Him we return. O Allah take me out of my plight and bring to me after it something better.","title":"Dua for Calamity (Masnoon Dua)","source":"Muslim: 918","reflection":"This dua for distress helps Muslims find hope and patience in tough times, asking Allah for reward and something better after every test or loss.","lesson":"Allah gives Sabr and reward to the one who makes dua for distress in calamity."},{"id":49,"text":"Allah is the Greatest, Most Great. Praise is to Allah, abundantly. Glory is to Allah, at the break of day and at its end.","title":"Dua before starting Salah","source":"Muslim: 601","reflection":"This dua before salat fills the heart with praise for Allah, helping Muslims start their Salah with Barakah and a strong focus on Iman and Amal.","lesson":"Allahu akbar kabira walhamdulillah kathira brings peace before every Salah."},{"id":50,"text":"Praise is to Allah, much, good and blessed praise.","title":"Dua at the Start of Salah","source":"Muslim: 600","reflection":"This before namaz dua fills the heart with praise for Allah and brings Barakah, making every Salah begin with thankfulness and a clean mind ready for worship.","lesson":"Allah gives more Barakah in Salah when muslims start with dua at the start of salah."},{"id":52,"text":"Our Lord, praise is Yours, abundant, good and blessed praise.","title":"Dua after Ruku (Rabana Lakal Hamdu)","source":"Bukhari: 799","reflection":"This dua after ruku fills your Salah with praise and thanks, bringing more Barakah and closeness to Allah, and making your namaz stronger with every word you say from the heart.","lesson":"Allah gives more Barakah in Salah when muslims say rabbana lakal hamd after ruku."},{"id":54,"text":"O Allah, our Lord and to You be the praise.","title":"Dua after Ruku (Rabana Lakal Hamdu)","source":"Bukhari: 796","reflection":"This after ruku dua brings more praise to Allah in Salah, making every rakah full of thanks and Barakah, and helps muslims keep their namaz strong and close to the Sunnah.","lesson":"Allah loves when muslims say rabbana lakal hamd after ruku in every Salah."},{"id":55,"text":"O Allah, I ask of You, O Allah, as You are the One, the Only, the Self-Sufficient Master, Who begets not nor was He begotten, and there is None equal or comparable to Him, forgive me my sins, for You are the Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","title":"Dua before Salam","source":"Sahih (Albani). Nasai: 1301","reflection":"This Salam Dua before ending Salah brings hope for forgiveness and mercy, letting every muslim ask Allah by His beautiful names and find peace in their heart before saying Salam.","lesson":"Allah forgives sins when muslims make this salam dua with true heart in namaz."},{"id":56,"text":"O Allah, I ask Thee by virtue of the fact that praise is due to Thee, there is no deity but Thou, Who showest favour and beneficence, the Originator of the Heavens and the earth, O Lord of Majesty and Splendour, O Living One, O Eternal One.","title":"Dua before Salam","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1495","reflection":"This dua after attahiyat fills the heart with praise for Allah, making Salah more strong and bringing hope for His help, mercy, and Barakah before saying Salam in every prayer.","lesson":"Allah gives more Barakah in Salah when muslims say this dua after attahiyat."},{"id":57,"text":"O Allah, I ask You, by the fact that I bear witness that You are Allah. There is none worthy of worship but You, the Only God, Independent of creation, who was not begotten and begets not, and none is equal to Him.","title":"Dua after Tashahhud (Dua Before Salam)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1493","reflection":"This dua after tashahhud makes Salah more strong by praising Allah’s oneness, helping Muslims ask for everything with a clean heart before saying Salam in every prayer.","lesson":"Allahumma inni as'aluka in this dua after tashahhud brings more Barakah in Salah."},{"id":58,"text":"I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah alone, Who has no partner; and I bear witness that Muhammad (ﷺ) is His slave and His Messenger.","title":"Dua after Wudu (Ablution)","source":"Muslim: 234","reflection":"This dua after ablution brings a Muslim closer to Allah, making every wudu more special and full of Barakah, while keeping the heart clean and the Iman strong for Salah and daily Amal.","lesson":"Allah opens all eight doors of Jannah for the one who says this dua after wudu."},{"id":59,"text":"None has the right to be worshiped except Allah, alone, without partner. To Him belongs sovereignty and all praise and He is over all things omnipotent.","title":"Dua on the Day of Arafah","source":"Hasan (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3585","reflection":"This dua on the day of Arafah brings a Muslim closer to Allah’s mercy, making the heart full of hope and Barakah, while the tongue stays busy with the best dhikr and praise for Allah.","lesson":"Allah forgives many sins for the one who makes this dua on the day of arafah."},{"id":68,"text":"None has the right to be worshipped but Allah. He is the Only One and has no partners. For Him is the Kingdom and all the praises are due for Him. He is Omnipotent. All the praises are for Allah. All the glories are for Allah. And none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, And Allah is Great And there is neither Might nor Power Except with Allah.","title":"Dua After Waking Up At Night (La Ilaha Illalahu Wa'hdahu)","source":"Bukhari: 1154","reflection":"This dua after waking up at night fills the heart with Allah’s praise and brings Barakah, making the night peaceful and the Iman strong for every Muslim who remembers Allah in the quiet hours.","lesson":"Allah gives special reward to the Muslim who says la ilaha illalahu after waking up."},{"id":72,"text":"There is none worthy of worship but You, glory is to You. Surely, I was among the wrongdoers.","title":"Dua of Yunus (La Ilaha Illa Anta Subhanaka)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3505","reflection":"This dua of Yunus brings hope and forgiveness for every Muslim, helping hearts find peace and Barakah, while making it easy to ask Allah for help in times of mushkil and sadness.","lesson":"Allah removes big troubles for the one who makes dua of Yunus with true heart."},{"id":73,"text":"We are from Allah and unto Him we return. O Allah take me out of my plight and bring to me after it something better.","title":"Dua for Hardship and Calamity","source":"Muslim: 918","reflection":"This dua for hardship and calamity helps a Muslim find peace and patience, bringing hope and Barakah from Allah when life feels heavy and the heart needs comfort in tough times.","lesson":"Allah gives better things to the one who says inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un."},{"id":74,"text":"O Allah, I ask You, by the fact that I bear witness that You are Allah. There is none worthy of worship but You, the Only God, Independent of creation, Who was not begotten and begets not, and none is equal to Him.","title":"Dua for Greatest Names of Allah (Ism-E-Azam)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Nasai: 1300","reflection":"This dua with the names of Allah brings a believer closer to Allah’s mercy and help, opening doors of Barakah and making the heart strong with Iman and hope in every part of life.","lesson":"Allah answers the names of Allah dua quickly when a Muslim calls with full Iman."},{"id":75,"text":"O Allah, I ask Thee by virtue of the fact that praise is due to Thee, there is no deity but Thou, Who showest favour and beneficence, the Originator of the Heavens and the earth, O Lord of Majesty and Splendour, O Living One, O Eternal One.","title":"Dua After Tashahhud (Allahumma inni as aluka)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Nasai: 1300","reflection":"This dua after attahiyat brings a Muslim closer to Allah’s mercy and help, making every namaz full of Barakah and hope by calling Allah with His beautiful names and praise.","lesson":"Allahumma inni as'aluka in tashahhud makes dua after namaz more accepted."},{"id":78,"text":"We have reached the morning and at this very time unto Allah, belongs all sovereignty, and all praise is for Allah. None has the right to be worshipped except Allah, alone, without any partner, to Him belong all sovereignty and praise and He is over all things omnipotent. My Lord, I ask You for the good of this day and the good of what follows it and I take refuge in You from the evil of this day and the evil of what follows it. My Lord, I take refuge in You from laziness and senility. My Lord, I take refuge in You from torment in the Fire and punishment in the grave.","title":"Morning Dua for Protection and Blessings","source":"","reflection":"Start your day with this morning dua to keep Allah’s Barakah close, asking for good things and safety from harm, making every morning full of hope and blessings for a Muslim.","lesson":"Asbahna wa asbahal mulku lillah keeps the heart safe from shaitan and evil."},{"id":79,"text":"We have reached the evening and at this very time unto Allah, belongs all sovereignty, and all praise is for Allah. None has the right to be worshipped except Allah, alone, without any partner, to Him belong all sovereignty and praise and He is over all things omnipotent. My Lord, I ask You for the good of this night and the good of what follows it and I take refuge in You from the evil of this night and the evil of what follows it. My Lord, I take refuge in You from laziness and senility. My Lord, I take refuge in You from torment in the Fire and punishment in the grave.","title":"Masnoon Evening Dua Recited by Prophet ﷺ","source":"Muslim: 2723","reflection":"This evening dua is a shield for Muslims, asking Allah for Barakah, protection from evil, and blessings in the night, just as the Prophet ﷺ did, bringing peace and safety to the heart before sleep.","lesson":"At sunset, recite evening dua for protection and blessings as night begins."},{"id":80,"text":"O Allah, by You we enter the morning and by You we enter the evening, by You we live and and by You we die, and to You is our resurrection.","title":"Morning Dua for Protection (Morning Azkar)","source":"","reflection":"Start your day with this morning dua for protection, asking Allah to keep you safe, bring Barakah, and guide your heart with His mercy from Fajr till night.","lesson":"Allahumma in this morning dua brings Hifazat and peace to the heart of a Muslim."},{"id":81,"text":"O Allah, by You we enter the evening and by You we enter the morning, by You we live and and by You we die, and to You is our resurrection","title":"Prayers for Evening (Masnun Dua)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 5068","reflection":"Find peace and safety as the sun sets by making this evening dua, asking Allah to keep your Iman strong and your family safe with His mercy and Barakah every night.","lesson":"Allahumma in this evening dua brings Hifazat and calmness to the heart at night."},{"id":82,"text":"We have reached the morning and at this very time all sovereignty belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds. O Allah, I ask You for the good of this day, its triumphs and its victories, its light and its blessings and its guidance, and I take refuge in You from the evil of this day and the evil that follows it.","title":"Dua in the morning for Blessings and Protection","source":"","reflection":"Start your day with this dua for the morning, asking Allah for Barakah, help, and safety, so your heart stays strong and your Amal gets light and guidance from Fajr till night.","lesson":"Asbahna wa asbahal mulku lillah brings Barkat and Noor in every new morning."},{"id":83,"text":"We have reached the evening and at this very time all sovereignty belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds. O Allah, I ask You for the good of this day, its triumphs and its victories, its light and its blessings and its guidance, and I take refuge in You from the evil of this day and the evil that follows it.","title":"Evening Dua for Guidance and Blessings","source":"Abu Dawud 4/322, No. 5084","reflection":"End your day with this evening dua for guidance and blessings, asking Allah to fill your night with Barakah, safety, and Noor, keeping your heart close to Him till morning.","lesson":"Amsaynaa wa amsal mulku lillah brings Barkat and peace in every night."},{"id":84,"text":"We rise in the morning upon the fitrah of Islaam, and the word of pure faith, and upon the religion of our Prophet Muhammad and the religion of our forefather Ibraaheem, who was a Muslim and of true faith and was not of those who associate others with Allah.","title":"Morning Dua for Islamic Fitrah (Masnun Dua)","source":"","reflection":"Start your day with this morning prayer, asking Allah to keep your Iman strong, your heart on the path of Islam, and your Amal pure like Nabi Ibrahim and Prophet Muhammad.","lesson":"Asbahnaa 'alaa fitratil-Islaami keeps a Muslim firm on Deen e Islam every morning."},{"id":85,"text":"We rise in the evening upon the fitrah of Islaam, and the word of pure faith, and upon the religion of our Prophet Muhammad and the religion of our forefather Ibraaheem, who was a Muslim and of true faith and was not of those who associate others with Allah.","title":"Evening Dua for Faith (Masnoon Dua)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Sahih Al Jame: 4674","reflection":"This evening prayer helps a Muslim keep Iman strong and pure, reminding us of the path of Muhammad and Nabi Ibrahim, and brings peace and Barakah to the heart every evening.","lesson":"Allah gives Barakah to the one who makes this evening prayer with true Iman."},{"id":86,"text":"I seek Allah's forgiveness and I turn to Him in repentance.","title":"Morning & Evening Istighfar Dua for Sins","source":"Bukhari: 6307, Muslim: 2702","reflection":"This morning evening adhkar brings a Muslim closer to Allah’s mercy, helping hearts stay clean and hopeful by asking for forgiveness and turning to Him with true tawbah every day.","lesson":"Allah forgives sins for the one who says this istighfar dua in morning evening adhkar."},{"id":87,"text":"How perfect Allah is! I praise Him by the number of His creation and His pleasure, and by the weight of His throne, and the ink of His words.","title":"Subhanallahi Wa Bihamdihi Dua (Morning dua)","source":"Muslim: 2726","reflection":"This dua of the morning fills the heart with praise for Allah, bringing peace and Barakah, and helps a Muslim remember His greatness and mercy from the start of the day.","lesson":"Subhanallahi wa bihamdihi brings endless Barakah in the morning for a Muslim."},{"id":88,"text":"O Allah, bestow Your favor on Muhammad (ﷺ) and on the family of Muhammad (ﷺ) as You have bestowed Your favor on Ibrahim (A) and on the family of Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Most Glorious. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You have blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Most Glorious.","title":"Dua For Morning & Evening (Durood Ibrahim)","source":"At-Tabrani, Sahih at-Targhib wa at-Tarhib 1/273","reflection":"Durood Ibrahim brings blessings to the heart and home, making every morning and evening full of Barakah, love for Muhammad, and closeness to Allah’s mercy.","lesson":"Durood ibrahim brings Allah’s Barakah to the one who sends it in morning and evening."},{"id":89,"text":"In the name of Allah with whose name nothing is harmed on earth nor in the heavens and He is The All-Seeing, The All-Knowing.","title":"Morning & Evening Dua for Protection","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 5088","reflection":"This dua for protection from harm keeps a Muslim safe by Allah’s name, making every morning and evening full of peace, safety, and trust in His power and knowledge.","lesson":"Bismillah keeps harm away from the one who says this dua for protection."},{"id":90,"text":"Allah is Sufficient for me, none has the right to be worshipped except Him, upon Him I rely and He is Lord of the exalted throne.","title":"Hasbiyallahu Dua (Morning & Evening Azkar)","source":"Sahih Maquf (Shu'aib and Arnaut). Abu Daud: 5081","reflection":"Start and end your day with this powerful morning and evening adhkar, trusting Allah’s care and mercy, and find peace in your heart by saying hasbiyallah with full Iman and hope.","lesson":"Allah is sufficient for me brings calmness and removes fear from the heart."},{"id":91,"text":"O Ever Living, O Self-Subsisting and Supporter of all, by Your mercy I seek assistance, rectify for me all of my affairs and do not leave me to myself, even for the blink of an eye.","title":"Ya Hayyu Ya Qayyum Full Dua (Morning Evening Azkar)","source":"Hasan (Albani). Silsilatul Sahiha: 227","reflection":"This azkar for morning and evening brings Allah’s mercy close, helps fix every problem, and keeps a Muslim safe from sadness and stress by calling on Ya Hayyu Ya Qayyum with full trust.","lesson":"Ya hayyu ya qayyum dua for morning and evening brings Allah’s help in every matter."},{"id":92,"text":"I am pleased with Allah as a Lord, and Islaam as a religion and Muhammad (ﷺ) as a Prophet.","title":"Morning & Evening Dua for Strong Iman","source":"Sahih li ghairihi (Shu’aib al-Arnaut). Takhrijul Musnad: 23112","reflection":"This dua for morning and evening fills the heart with Iman, brings peace, and helps a Muslim stay happy with Allah, Islam, and the Prophet, making every day better with strong faith.","lesson":"Saying this dua for morning and evening keeps Iman strong in the heart."},{"id":93,"text":"O Allah, I gave my honour As Charity/Sadaka to thy servants.","title":"Morning & Evening Dua for Forgiveness","source":"Sahih Maktu (Albani). Abu Dawud: 4886","reflection":"This dua for forgiveness in morning and evening helps a Muslim let go of anger, brings Allah’s mercy, and fills the heart with peace by giving honour as sadqah for others.","lesson":"Allahumma inni dua for forgiveness wipes away sins and brings maghfirat."},{"id":95,"text":"O Allah, You are my Lord, none has the right to be worshipped except You, You created me and I am Your servant and I abide to Your covenant and promise as best I can, I take refuge in You from the evil of which I have committed. I acknowledge Your favour upon me and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for verily none can forgive sin except You.","title":"Best Dua For Forgiveness (Sayyidul Istigfar)","source":"Bukhari: 6306","reflection":"This powerful dua, known as sayyidul istigfar, brings hope and mercy to every Muslim who seeks Allah’s forgiveness with a true heart and wants to keep Iman strong every day.","lesson":"Allah’s mercy covers the one who makes sayyidul istigfar with a true heart."},{"id":96,"text":"Allah! There is none worthy of worship but He, the Ever Living, the One Who sustains and protects all that exists. Neither slumber nor sleep overtakes Him. To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. Who is he that can intercede with Him except with His Permission? He knows what happens to them in this world, and what will happen to them in the Hereafter. And they will never compass anything of His Knowledge except that which He wills. His Throne extends over the heavens and the earth, and He feels no fatigue in guarding and preserving them. And He is the Most High, the Most Great.","title":"Ayatul Kursi -The Throne Verse (Masnun Dua)","source":"Bukhari: 2311","reflection":"Ayatul kursi brings strong safety and peace from Allah, making every Muslim feel safe and close to Him when this verse is read with Iman and hope in the heart.","lesson":"Allah’s hifazat covers the one who keeps ayatul kursi close after every Salah."},{"id":99,"text":"Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers who preceded us in faith and put not in our hearts [any] resentment toward those who have believed. Our Lord, indeed You are Kind and Merciful.","title":"Dua for Protection from Hatred","source":"Surah Hashr 59:10","reflection":"This dua for forgiveness from surah hashr helps keep the heart clean and brings Allah’s kindness, making every Muslim feel peace and love for others in daily life.","lesson":"Allah’s mercy covers the one who makes this dua for forgiveness with Iman."},{"id":100,"text":"O Allah, grant my body health, O Allah, grant my hearing health, O Allah, grant my sight health. None has the right to be worshipped except You. O Allah, I take refuge with You from disbelief and poverty, and I take refuge with You from the punishment of the grave. None has the right to be worshipped except You.","title":"Dua in The Morning & Evening (Dua For Health)","source":"Hasan (Albani). Abu Dawud: 5090","reflection":"Start your day and end it with this dua for health, asking Allah for strong body, good hearing, clear sight, and safety from harm, poverty, disbelief, and the punishment of the grave.","lesson":"Allahumma afini fi badani keeps a Muslim’s body safe from sickness and pain."},{"id":101,"text":"O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Creator of the heavens and the Earth, Lord and Sovereign of all things, I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped except You. I take refuge in You from the evil of my soul and from the evil and shirk of the devil, and from committing wrong against my soul or bringing such upon another Muslim.","title":"Morning Dua for Evil Protection","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3529","reflection":"Start your morning with this dua for protection, asking Allah to keep you safe from your own mistakes, the harm of shaitan, and any evil that can touch you or other Muslims.","lesson":"Allahumma shields a Muslim from shaitan’s evil and his shirk in daily life."},{"id":102,"text":"O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in this life and the next. O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religious and worldly affairs, and my family and my wealth. O Allah, veil my weaknesses and set at ease my dismay. O Allah, preserve me from the front and from behind and on my right and on my left and from above, and I take refuge with You lest I be swallowed up by the earth.","title":"Dua For Pardon And Well-Being","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 5074","reflection":"Ask Allah for forgiveness, safety, and protection in every part of life with this dua, covering your deen, family, wealth, and all sides from harm in this world and the next.","lesson":"Allahumma inni as aluka brings Allah’s maghfirat and covers all mistakes."},{"id":104,"text":"I take refuge in Allah's perfect words from the evil He has created.","title":"Dua For Protection From Insects (Auzu Bikalimatillahi Tammati)","source":"Muslim: 2708, 2709","reflection":"Say this dua for protection from insects and all harm, asking Allah to keep you safe from every evil thing He has made, using His perfect words for your safety and peace.","lesson":"Auzu bikalimatillahi tammati keeps Muslims safe from insects and hidden harm."},{"id":106,"text":"O Allah, verily I have reached the morning and call on You, the bearers of Your throne, Your angels, and all of Your creation to witness that You are Allah, none has the right to be worshipped except You, alone, without any partner and that Muhammad is Your Servant and Messenger.","title":"Powerful Morning Dua (Allahumma Inni Asbahtu)","source":"","reflection":"Start your day with this powerful morning dua to keep Iman strong, seek Allah’s help, and bring Barakah and safety for you and your family in every step you take from morning till night.","lesson":"Allahumma in this dua for morning makes Iman fresh and keeps heart close to Allah."},{"id":107,"text":"O Allah, what blessing I have received in this morning or any of Your creation, is from You alone, without any partner, so for You is all praise and unto You all thanks.","title":"Dua for the Morning (Allahumma Ma Asbaha)","source":"","reflection":"Begin your day with this dua in the morning to thank Allah for every blessing, keep your heart full of Alhamdulillah, and remember His gifts with every breath you take from sunrise.","lesson":"Allahuma in this morning dua helps Muslims show shukr for every ni’mah."},{"id":108,"text":"O Allah, I ask You for knowledge which is beneficial and sustenance which is good, and deeds which are acceptable.","title":"Morning Dua for Rizq and Knowledge","source":"Sahih (Albani). Ibn Majah: 925","reflection":"Ask Allah with this dua for rizq and knowledge to fill your day with halal wealth, useful ilm, and good Amal that brings Barakah and makes your life easy in every way.","lesson":"Allahumma in this morning dua brings pure rizq and makes Amal strong."},{"id":109,"text":"O Allah, verily I have reached evening and call on You, the bearers of Your throne, Your angels, and all of Your creation to witness that You are Allah, none has the right to be worshipped except You, alone, without any partner and that Muhammad is Your Servant and Messenger.","title":"Allahumma Inni Dua (Evening Adhkar)","source":"Hasan (Ibn Baz). Abu Dawud: 5069","reflection":"End your day with this dua for evening to keep Iman safe, remember Allah’s oneness, and ask for His mercy and protection as night comes and you rest from your daily Amal.","lesson":"Allahuma in this evening dua keeps Iman strong and heart close to Allah."},{"id":110,"text":"Glory be to Allah and His is the praise, (and) Allah, the Greatest is free from imperfection","title":"Best Dhikr and Dua (SubhanAllah wa Bihamdihi)","source":"Bukhari: 6682","reflection":"Keep your tongue busy with SubhanAllah wa Bihamdihi to earn Allah’s love, get sins forgiven, and fill your day with Barakah and peace from the best dhikr and dua in Islam.","lesson":"Subhanallah wa bihamdihi meaning brings Allah’s praise and keeps heart clean."},{"id":111,"text":"O Allah forgive me, and have mercy on me and guide me and give me good health and provide rizq for me.","title":"Powerful Dua for Forgiveness & Rizq","source":"Muslim: 2697","reflection":"This dua for forgiveness and rizq brings hope for mercy, guidance, health, and halal wealth, making it a trusted prayer for every muslim seeking Allah’s help in daily life.","lesson":"Allahumma forgives all sins and brings Barakah in rizq for the one who asks."},{"id":112,"text":"None has the right to be worshiped but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs all sovereignty and to Him is the praise, He gives life and gives death, and He is Ever-Living and does not die; in His Hand is all goodness and He is Able to do all things.","title":"Dua for Entering the Market (Masnun Dua)","source":"Hasan (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3428","reflection":"This dua entering market brings Allah’s remembrance to busy places, helping muslims keep their Iman strong and seek Barakah and safety in every business and daily work.","lesson":"La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu brings huge Barakah in business."},{"id":116,"text":"Allah! There is none worthy of worship but He, the Ever Living, the One Who sustains and protects all that exists. Neither slumber nor sleep overtakes Him. To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. Who is he that can intercede with Him except with His Permission? He knows what happens to them in this world, and what will happen to them in the Hereafter. And they will never compass anything of His Knowledge except that which He wills. His Throne extends over the heavens and the earth, and He feels no fatigue in guarding and preserving them. And He is the Most High, the Most Great. (Sura Baqarah 2:255)","title":"Dua Before Sleep (Ayatul Kursi)","source":"Al-Bukhari, Fathul Bari 4/487, no. 2311","reflection":"Let your heart rest easy before going to bed by saying Ayatul Kursi, a strong verse from Surah Baqarah that brings Allah’s care, safety, and peace to every Muslim’s night.","lesson":"Allah’s hifazat covers the one who says ayatul kursi before going to bed."},{"id":118,"text":"(1) Say, \"O disbelievers, (2) I do not worship what you worship. (3) Nor are you worshippers of what I worship. (4) Nor will I be a worshipper of what you worship. (5) Nor will you be worshippers of what I worship. (6) For you is your religion, and for me is my religion.\" (Sura kafirun 109: 1-6)","title":"Dua Before Going to Bed (Surah Kafirun)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3403","reflection":"Let your heart rest easy before going to bed by saying surah kafirun, a strong night dua that keeps your iman safe and brings Allah’s help and peace to every muslim.","lesson":"Surah kafirun keeps a muslim’s iman pure from shirk before sleep."},{"id":122,"text":"O Allah, in Your Name I die and I live.","title":"Dua for Sleeping","source":"Bukhari: 6314","reflection":"Let your heart rest easy by saying this dua for sleeping, trusting Allah to keep you safe and wake you up with His Barakah and mercy every night and morning.","lesson":"Allahumma bismika amutu wa ahya brings peace to the heart before going to bed."},{"id":123,"text":"In Your name O Allah, I live and die.","title":"Before Sleep Dua","source":"Al-Bukhari, Fathul Bari 11/113 no. 6324, Muslim 4/2083 no. 2711","reflection":"Let your mind and body rest by saying this dua for sleep, trusting Allah to give you a peaceful night and wake you up with His mercy and Barakah every morning.","lesson":"Bismika allahumma amutu wa ahya keeps a Muslim safe from harm during the night."},{"id":124,"text":"Praise be to Allah Who has given me sufficiency, has guarded me, given me food and drink, been most gracious to me, and given to me most lavishly. Praise be to Allah in every circumstance. O Allah! Lord and King of everything, God of everything, I seek refuge in Thee from Hell.","title":"Dua for Going to Sleep","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 5058","reflection":"Show thanks to Allah with this dua for going to sleep, remembering His gifts and asking for His protection and mercy before you rest at night.","lesson":"Alhamdulillah ala kulli hal fills the heart with shukr for every blessing from Allah."},{"id":125,"text":"O Allah, verily You have created my soul and You shall take it's life, to You belong it's life and death. If You keep my soul alive then protect it, and if You take it's life then forgive it. O Allah, I ask You to grant me good health.","title":"Dua to Go to Sleep","source":"Muslim: 2712","reflection":"Trust Allah with your soul by making this dua to go to sleep, asking for His protection, forgiveness, and good health before you rest for the night.","lesson":"Allahumma inni as aluka in this dua to go to sleep brings safety for the soul."},{"id":126,"text":"O Allah You are the First and nothing has come before you, and You are the Last, and nothing may come after You. You are the Most High, nothing is above You and You are the Most Near and nothing is nearer than You. Remove our debts from us and enrich us against poverty.","title":"Dua to Read Before Sleeping","source":"Muslim: 2713","reflection":"Feel close to Allah by saying this dua before sleeping, trusting Him to remove your worries, debts, and give you Barakah and peace before you rest at night.","lesson":"Allahumma in this dua before sleeping reminds a Muslim of Allah’s greatness."},{"id":127,"text":"O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and the Lord of the Earth and Lord of the Magnificent Throne, our Lord and Lord of all things, Splitter of the seed and the date stone, Revealer of the Towraat, the Injeel and the Furqaan, I take refuge in You from the evil of all things You shall seize by the forelock. O Allah, You are The First so there is nothing before You and You are The Last so there is nothing after You. You are ath-Dhaahir so there is nothing above You and You are al-Baatin so there is nothing closer than You. Settle our debt for us and spare us from poverty.","title":"Dua to Say Before Sleeping","source":"Muslim: 2713, Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3481","reflection":"Let your heart rest easy by making this dua to say before sleeping, asking Allah for safety, help with debt, and peace in your night, trusting His power and mercy before going to bed.","lesson":"Allahumma in this dua before sleeping brings Barakah and calm to the heart."},{"id":128,"text":"I seek refuge in the Perfect Words of Allah from His anger and His punishment, from the evil of His slaves and from the taunts of devils and from their presence.","title":"Dua of Sleeping","source":"Hasan (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3528","reflection":"This dua of sleeping helps a Muslim find peace and safety at night, asking Allah to protect from harm, shayateen, and His anger before going to bed with a calm heart.","lesson":"Audhubillah in this dua for protection keeps Allah’s anger and azaab away."},{"id":129,"text":"In Your name my Lord, I lie down and in Your name I rise, so if You should take my soul then have mercy upon it, and if You should return my soul then protect it in the manner You do so with Your righteous servants.","title":"Dua of Sleep","source":"Al-Bukhari 11/126 no. 6320, Muslim 4/2084 no.2714","reflection":"This dua of sleep lets a Muslim trust Allah with their soul before going to bed, asking for His mercy and care, just like He gives to His good servants every night.","lesson":"Bismika rabbi in this sleeping dua brings peace and safety to the heart."},{"id":130,"text":"O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day Your servants are resurrected.","title":"Dua Before Going to Bed","source":"Sahih (Albani). At-Tirmizi: 3398","reflection":"This dua before going to bed helps a Muslim ask Allah for safety from His punishment on the Day of Qiyamah, bringing peace and hope before sleep every night.","lesson":"Allahumma in this dua before sleep asks Allah to save from azaab in akhirah."},{"id":131,"text":"O my Lord, I have slept in your name. You forgive my sins.","title":"Dua to Sleep","source":"Hasan (Shuaib al-Arnait). Musnad Ahmad: 6620","reflection":"This dua to sleep lets a Muslim ask Allah for forgiveness and peace before going to bed, trusting His mercy and kindness every night with a simple heart.","lesson":"Bismika Rabbi in this sleeping dua brings Allah’s mercy close to the heart."},{"id":132,"text":"All praise is for Allah, Who fed us and gave us drink, and Who is sufficient for us and has sheltered us, for how many have none to suffice them or shelter them.","title":"Sleeping Dua","source":"Muslim 4/2085 no. 2715","reflection":"This sleeping dua reminds us to thank Allah for food, water, shelter, and His care, filling our hearts with Alhamdulillah before sleep and teaching us to trust Allah’s mercy every night.","lesson":"All praise is for Allah, Who fed us and gave us drink, and Who is sufficient for us and has sheltered us, for how many have none to suffice them or shelter them."},{"id":133,"text":"O Allah, Knower of the seen and the unseen, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Lord and Sovereign of all things I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped except You. I take refuge in You from the evil of my soul and from the evil and shirk of the devil, and from committing wrong against my soul or bringing such upon another Muslim.","title":"Duas Before Sleeping","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3392","reflection":"These duas before sleeping help protect your Iman and heart from harm, reminding you to trust Allah, seek His help, and keep away from shaytan’s tricks every night before you rest.","lesson":"O Allah, Knower of the seen and the unseen, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Lord and Sovereign of all things."},{"id":134,"text":"I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, which no virtuous person or sinner can overcome, from the evil of what He has created, created and spread, from the evil of that which descends from heaven, from the evil of that which ascends to heaven. From the evil of whatever is scattered in the earth, from the evil of whatever comes out of the earth, from the evil of the fitnah of night and day, and from the evil of all strangers, except the one who comes with goodness, O Most Merciful.","title":"Duas Before Sleep","source":"Sahih (Arnaut). Ahmed: 15499","reflection":"These duas before sleep help you ask Allah the most merciful for safety from harm, fitnah, and all evil, filling your heart with peace and trust in Ar Rahman every night before you rest.","lesson":"I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, which no virtuous person or sinner can overcome."},{"id":135,"text":"In the name of Allah, I have laid down my side for Allah. O Allah! forgive my sin, drive away my devil, free me from my responsibility, and place me in the highest assembly.","title":"Duas Before Bed","source":"Sahih (Albani). Sunan Abu Dawud: 5054","reflection":"These duas before bed help you ask Allah for forgiveness, Barakah, and safety from shaytan, making your heart calm and your Iman strong before you sleep every night.","lesson":"Bismillah and Allahumma bring peace and forgiveness before sleep."},{"id":136,"text":"O Allah, I submit my soul unto You, and I entrust my affair unto You, and I turn my face towards You, and I totally rely on You, in hope and fear of You. Verily there is no refuge nor safe haven from You except with You. I believe in Your Book which You have revealed and in Your Prophet whom You have sent.","title":"Dua Before Bed","source":"Al-Bukhari, Fathul Bari 11/113 no. 6313, Muslim 4/2081 no. 2710","reflection":"This dua before bed is a strong shield for your heart and mind, helping you trust Allah, find peace, and ask for protection as you rest, following the Sunnah and building Iman every night.","lesson":"Allahumma aslamtu nafsi ilaika teaches full trust in Allah before sleep."},{"id":138,"text":"There is none worthy of worship but Allah, the One, the Victorious, Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them, the All-Mighty, the All-Forgiving.","title":"Dua When Turning Over During the Night","source":"Sahih by Hakim. Imam Dhahabi 1/540; Nasai, Amalul Yaomi Wallayla No. 202, Ibnus sunni No. 757. Also see, Sahih Jame 4:213","reflection":"This dua when turning over during the night helps you remember Allah’s greatness, brings Barakah to your sleep, and keeps your heart close to Iman even in the quietest hours.","lesson":"There is none worthy of worship but Allah, the One, the Victorious, Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them, the All-Mighty, the All-Forgiving."},{"id":139,"text":"None has the right to be worshipped except Allah, alone, without any partner, to Him belong sovereignty and praise and He is over all things wholly capable. How perfect Allah is, and all praise is for Allah, and none has the right to be worshipped except Allah, Allah is the greatest and there is no power nor might except with Allah, The Most High, The Supreme, O my Lord forgive me.","title":"Dua for Waking Up","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 5060","reflection":"This dua for waking up fills your morning with Barakah, brings you closer to Allah, and helps you start your day with Iman, forgiveness, and the zikr of Allah on your tongue.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah and forgiveness at the start of the day."},{"id":141,"text":"All praise is for Allah who gave us life after having taken it from us and unto Him is the resurrection.","title":"Dua After Waking Up","source":"Al-Bukhari, cf. Al-Asqalani, Fathul-Bari 11/113 no. 6314; Muslim 4/2083 no. 2711","reflection":"This dua after waking up fills your heart with Alhamdulillah, brings Barakah to your morning, and reminds you of Allah’s mercy as you start a new day with Iman and hope for a good day ahead.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah and gratitude at the start of the day."},{"id":142,"text":"Praise is to Allah Who gave strength to my body and returned my soul to me and permitted me to remember Him.","title":"Dua For Waking Up For Fajr","source":"At-Tirmithi 5/473. See Al-Albani's Sahih Tirmiihi 3/144","reflection":"This dua for waking up for fajr fills your heart with shukr to Allah for giving you life, health, and the chance to remember Him at fajr time, bringing Barakah and strength to your day from the very start.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah and health at the start of fajr."},{"id":144,"text":"I seek refuge in Allah from Satan the outcast.","title":"Dua for Bad Dreams","source":"[1] Bukhari: 7044 [2] Muslim: 6041 [3] Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 2280","reflection":"Dua for Bad Dreams helps you seek Allah’s protection from shaitan, brings calm and safety to your heart after a nightmare, and reminds you to trust Allah’s mercy in every moment of fear.","lesson":"Reciting this dua after a bad dream brings Allah’s protection from shaitan."},{"id":146,"text":"All Praise is for Allah who has clothed me with this garment and provided it for me, with no power nor might from myself.","title":"Dua When Wearing Clothes","source":"Hasan (Albani). Abu Dawud: 4023","reflection":"Dua when wearing clothes reminds you to thank Allah for every garment, showing shukr for His Rizq and remembering that all blessings come from Him alone, not from our own power or strength.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah in every dress you wear."},{"id":147,"text":"O Allah, for You is all praise, You have clothed me with it, I ask You for the good of it and the good for which it was made, and I seek refuge with You from the evil of it and the evil for which it was made.","title":"Dua for Wearing New Clothes","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 1767","reflection":"Dua for wearing new clothes helps you thank Allah for His gifts, asking for good from your new dress and seeking safety from any harm, filling your heart with shukr and Barakah every time you wear something new.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah and protection in new clothes."},{"id":148,"text":"May you wear it out and Allah (Ta'aala) replace it [with another].","title":"Dua for Someone Wearing New Clothes","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 4020","reflection":"Dua for someone wearing new clothes is a way to make Barakah for others, asking Allah to bless their new dress and give them more, filling hearts with love and shukr for every gift from Allah.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah and happiness to others."},{"id":150,"text":"May you live so long that your dress gets worn out.","title":"Dua for Someone Wearing New Clothes (Female)","source":"Bukhari: 5993","reflection":"Dua for someone wearing new clothes is a way to ask Allah for long life, Barakah, and happiness for the sister or mother, wishing her to enjoy her dress until it gets old with Iman and Amal.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah and happiness for sisters and mothers."},{"id":151,"text":"May you live so long that your dress gets worn out.","title":"Dua for Someone Wearing New Clothes (Male)","source":"Bukhari: 5993","reflection":"Dua for someone wearing new clothes is a simple way to ask Allah for a long life and Barakah for your brother, father, or son, wishing him to enjoy his new dress until it gets old with Iman and happiness.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah and happiness for brothers, fathers, and sons."},{"id":152,"text":"Wear anew, live commendably and die a shaheed.","title":"Dua When Someone Wearing New Dress","source":"Sahih (Albani). Ibn Majah: 3558","reflection":"Dua to wear new clothes asks Allah for a good life, Barakah, and the honor of dying as a shaheed, wishing the person to enjoy their new dress with Iman and Amal every time they wear something fresh.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah and good wishes for the person wearing new clothes."},{"id":153,"text":"Wear anew, live commendably and die a shaheed and may Allah give you those things in this duniya and in hereafter which will cool your eyes.","title":"Dua Said To Someone Wearing New Clothes","source":"Sahih (Albani). Sahihul Jami: 1234","reflection":"Dua for new clothes asks Allah to give a good life, Barakah, and coolness of eyes in both duniya and akhirah, wishing the person to enjoy their new dress with Iman and happiness every time they wear it.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah and happiness for the person wearing new clothes."},{"id":154,"text":"In the name of Allah, I place my trust in Allah and there is no might nor power except with Allah.","title":"Dua for leaving home","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 5095","reflection":"Dua for leaving home reminds every Muslim to trust Allah, seek His help, and ask for Barakah and safety before stepping out, making every journey start with Iman and hope in Allah’s care.","lesson":"Reciting this dua brings Barakah and protection before leaving home."},{"id":155,"text":"In the Name of Allah, I place my trust in Allah. O Allah! We seek refuge in You from slipping unintentionally or becoming misguided, or committing oppression or being oppressed, or acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly.","title":"Dua before leaving house","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3427","reflection":"Dua before leaving house helps Muslims start their day with Iman, asking Allah for Barakah, safety from harm, and protection from mistakes or being wronged while outside.","lesson":"Dua before leaving house brings Allah’s help and covers you with His protection."},{"id":156,"text":"O Allah, I seek refuge with You lest I should stray or be led astray, or slip (i.e. to commit a sin unintentionally) or be tripped, or oppress or be oppressed, or behave foolishly or be treated foolishly.","title":"Dua when leaving the house","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 5094","reflection":"This dua when leaving the house is a strong shield for Muslims, asking Allah for Barakah, safety from mistakes, and protection from harm or being wronged as you step outside with Iman.","lesson":"Dua when leaving the house protects from going astray or being led astray."},{"id":157,"text":"O Allah! I ask Thee for good both when entering and when going out; in the name of Allah we have entered, and in the name of Allah we have gone out, and in Allah our Lord do we trust.","title":"Dua for entering home","source":"Hasan (Ibn Baz). Abu Dawud: 5096","reflection":"Dua for entering home brings Barakah and peace, asking Allah for good, safety, and trust in Him every time you step inside, making your house a place of Iman and comfort.","lesson":"Dua for entering home brings Allah’s Barakah and safety to your house."},{"id":158,"text":"Peace be upon you, and the Mercy of Allah and His Blessings.","title":"Dua before entering home","source":"Hasan (Ibn Hajar). MIshkat: 4/316","reflection":"Bring peace and Barakah to your house by saying this dua before entering home, letting Allah’s mercy and blessings fill your family and protect everyone inside from harm and trouble.","lesson":"Saying assalamualaikum warahmatullahi wabarakatuh brings Allah’s Barakah to the home."},{"id":159,"text":"In the name of Allah we enter and in the name of Allah we leave, and upon our Lord we place our trust.","title":"Dua of entering home","source":"[1] Hasan (Ibn Baz). Abu Dawud: 5096 [2] Muslim: 2018","reflection":"Let your house be filled with Allah’s care and trust by saying this dua of entering home, making every step inside and outside safe with His name and keeping your family close to His Rahmah.","lesson":"Bismillah in this dua for entering home keeps shaytan away from your house."},{"id":160,"text":"In the Name of Allah. O Allah, I seek protection in You from the male and female unclean spirits.","title":"Dua Before Entering the Toilet","source":"Bukhari: 142","reflection":"Keep yourself safe from harm and impurity by saying this dua before entering the toilet, letting Allah’s name protect you from all evil and keeping your heart clean and full of Iman.","lesson":"Bismillah in this dua before entering the toilet keeps shayateen away from you."},{"id":163,"text":"I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped except Allah, alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger (ﷺ). I am pleased with Allah as a Lord, and Muhammad as a Messenger and Islam as a religion.","title":"Dua after hearing Adhan (Azan dua)","source":"Muslim: 386","reflection":"Let your Iman grow strong by saying the azan dua after hearing the call to prayer, showing love for Allah, His Messenger, and Islam, and bringing Barakah to your Salah and daily Amal.","lesson":"Ash hadu allah ilaha illallah in azan dua makes Iman shine in the heart."},{"id":164,"text":"O Allah, bestow Your favor on Muhammad (ﷺ) and on the family of Muhammad (ﷺ) as You have bestowed Your favor on Ibrahim (Ah) and on the family of Ibrahim (Ah), You are Praiseworthy, Most Glorious. O Allah, bless Muhammad (ﷺ) and the family of Muhammad (ﷺ) as You have blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim (Ah), You are Praiseworthy, Most Glorious.","title":"Dua After Adhan (Durood Sharif)","source":"Muslim: 384","reflection":"This dua after azan brings blessings and mercy from Allah, raising the rank of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ and his family, and brings Barakah to those who send durood sharif after hearing the call to prayer.","lesson":"Allah gives Barakah to the one who sends durood sharif after azan."},{"id":165,"text":"O Allah, Owner of this perfect call and Owner of this prayer to be performed, bestow upon Muhammad (ﷺ) al-waseelah and al-fadeelah and raise him upon a praised platform which You have promised him.","title":"Dua After Adhan (Azan Dua)","source":"Bukhari: 614","reflection":"This dua after adhan brings special rewards, helps raise the rank of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, and brings Barakah and acceptance for those who remember Allah after hearing the azan.","lesson":"Allah grants the promise of Maqam Mahmood to Prophet Muhammad ﷺ."},{"id":168,"text":"O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins.","title":"Dua for Imams and Mu'adhdhins (Dua for Forgiveness)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 517","reflection":"This dua for imams and mu'adhdhins brings Allah’s guidance for leaders and forgiveness for those who call to prayer, making the masjid a place of Barakah and unity for all muslims.","lesson":"Allahumma gives hidayah to imams so they lead Salah with true Iman."},{"id":170,"text":"I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah alone, Who has no partner; and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and His Messenger (ﷺ).","title":"Dua After Wudu (Ablution)","source":"Muslim: 234 , 576","reflection":"This dua after wudu makes a muslim’s Iman strong, brings Barakah to every Salah, and helps keep the heart clean by remembering Allah and the truth of Muhammad ﷺ as His Messenger.","lesson":"Ash hadu alla ilaha illallah after wudu brings more reward for every Amal."},{"id":171,"text":"O Allah, make me among those who turn to You in repentance, and make me among those who are purified.","title":"After Wudu Dua (Ablution)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 55","reflection":"This after wudu dua brings a muslim closer to Allah by asking for forgiveness and purity, making every ablution a chance to earn Barakah and keep the heart clean for Salah and Amal.","lesson":"Allahumma in this after wudu dua helps a muslim get Barakah in every Salah."},{"id":172,"text":"Glory is to You, O Allah, and praise; I bear witness that there is none worthy of worship but You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.","title":"Dua After Ablution (Wudu Dua)","source":"An-Nasa'i, 'Amalul-Yawm wal-Laylah, p. 173. See also Al-Albani, 'Irwa'ul-Ghalil 1/135 and 2/94.","reflection":"This dua after ablution helps a muslim remember Allah’s greatness and ask for forgiveness, making every wudu a time to clean the heart and get ready for Salah with Barakah and Iman.","lesson":"Subhanaka allahumma wa bihamdika in this dua after ablution brings Barakah."},{"id":173,"text":"O Allah, place within my heart light, and upon my tongue light, and within my ears light, and within my eyes light, and place behind me light, and in front of me light, and above me light, and beneath me light. O Allah, bestow upon me light.","title":"Dua for going to the Mosque (Dua e noor)","source":"Bukhari: 6316","reflection":"This dua for going to the mosque fills a muslim’s heart and life with Allah’s noor, making every step to the masjid a way to get Barakah, light, and blessings in Amal and Iman.","lesson":"Allahumma in dua e noor brings light to the heart and makes Amal shine bright."},{"id":174,"text":"O Allah, place light in my heart, and on my tongue light, and in my ears light and in my sight light, and above me light, and below me light, and to my right light, and to my left light, and before me light and behind me light. Place in my soul light. Magnify for me light, and amplify for me light. Make for me light and make me a light. O Allah, grant me light, and place light in my nerves, and in my body light and in my blood light and in my hair light and in my skin light.","title":"Dua For Going To The Masjid","source":"Bukhari: 6316","reflection":"This dua for going to the masjid fills a muslim’s heart, body, and soul with Allah’s noor, making every step to the mosque a way to get Barakah, light, and blessings in Amal and Iman.","lesson":"Allahumma in dua of light brings noor to every part of the body and heart."},{"id":175,"text":"In the Name of Allah, And blessings and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). O Allah, open before me the doors of Your mercy.","title":"Dua When Entering Masjid (Wassalatu Wassalamu)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 465, Muslim: 713","reflection":"This dua when entering masjid brings a muslim under Allah’s mercy and blessings, making every step inside the mosque a way to get Barakah, peace, and closeness to Rasulullah (peace be upon him).","lesson":"Bismillah in dua for entering masjid brings Barakah and safety at every step."},{"id":176,"text":"In the Name of Allah, Ya Allah please send blessings and peace upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). O Allah, open before me the doors of Your mercy.","title":"Dua For Entering Mosque (Allahumma Salli Ala Muhammad)","source":"Hasan (Albani). Ibn Sunni: 88, Muslim: 713","reflection":"Entering the mosque with this dua brings Allah’s mercy closer, helps keep your heart clean, and reminds you to honor the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ every time you step inside.","lesson":"Allahumma salli ala muhammad in this dua for entering mosque brings Barakah."},{"id":177,"text":"O Allah, forgive me my sins and open to me the gates of Your mercy.","title":"Dua To Enter Mosque (Rabbighfirli dhunubi)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Ibn Majah: 771","reflection":"This dua to enter mosque asks Allah for forgiveness and mercy, making your heart ready for Salah and helping you start your time in the masjid with a clean soul and hope for Barakah.","lesson":"Rabbighfirli in dua before entering mosque brings Allah’s Maghfirat closer."},{"id":178,"text":"I take refuge with Allah, The Supreme and with His Noble Face, and His eternal authority from the accursed devil. In the name of Allah, and prayers and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). O Allah, open the gates of Your mercy for me.","title":"Dua Before Entering The Mosque (Auzubillah)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 465, 466","reflection":"This dua before entering the mosque keeps shaytan away, brings Allah’s mercy, and helps you start your masjid time with a clean heart and love for the Prophet ﷺ.","lesson":"Auzubillah in dua entering mosque gives strong hifazat from shaytan’s waswasah."},{"id":179,"text":"In the name of Allah (I am going out).Oh Allah! Please send bessings and peace upon muhammad (ﷺ). Oh Allah! I want from your bounty.","title":"Dua For Leaving Masjid (Allahumma Inni As Aluka)","source":"Hasan (Albani). Ibn Sunni: 88, Muslim: 713","reflection":"This dua for leaving mosque asks Allah for His bounty, keeps the Prophet ﷺ in your heart, and helps you step out with Barakah and hope for more good deeds in your daily life.","lesson":"Allahumma inni as aluka in masjid leaving dua brings Allah’s Fazl in daily Amal."},{"id":180,"text":"In the Name of Allah, and peace and blessings be upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). O Allah, I ask for Your favor, O Allah, protect me from Satan the outcast.","title":"Dua When Leaving Masjid (Wassalatu Wassalamu)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Ibn Majah: 773","reflection":"This leaving mosque dua asks Allah for His favor, keeps shaitan away, and helps you step out with peace, remembering the Prophet ﷺ and holding Barakah in your daily Amal.","lesson":"Bismillah in dua for leaving mosque keeps Iman safe and Amal strong outside."},{"id":181,"text":"O Allah, protect me from Satan the outcast.","title":"Dua Upon Leaving The Mosque (Allahumma Ajirni)","source":"Sahih (Ibn Hibban). Ibn Hibban: 2047","reflection":"As you step out from the masjid, this dua keeps you safe from shaitan’s tricks and brings Allah’s help, making your way home and daily life filled with His Barakah and care.","lesson":"Allahumma ajirni minannar keeps a Muslim safe from shaitan’s waswasah."},{"id":182,"text":"O Allah, protect me from Satan the outcast.","title":"Leaving Mosque Dua","source":"Sahih (Albani). Ibn Majah: 773","reflection":"When a Muslim leaves the masjid, this dua asks Allah to keep shaitan away and brings peace, making every step outside filled with His care and safety for the day ahead.","lesson":"Allahumma keeps the heart safe from shaitan’s evil after leaving mosque."},{"id":183,"text":"O Lord pardon my sins, and open the gates of Your blessings for me.","title":"Masjid Leaving Dua (Allahummaghfirli)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Ibn Majah: 771","reflection":"As you walk out from the masjid, this dua asks Allah for forgiveness and His gifts, making your day brighter with Barakah, mercy, and doors of goodness opening for you.","lesson":"Allahummaghfirli helps a Muslim get forgiveness for sins after Salah."},{"id":184,"text":"May Allah not return it to you.","title":"Dua for the one who announces lost items in the mosque","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 1321","reflection":"This mosque dua teaches respect for Allah’s house and keeps the masjid peaceful, reminding Muslims to follow the right way when something is lost or missing inside the mosque.","lesson":"Mosque dua helps keep the masjid safe from loud calls about lost and found."},{"id":185,"text":"May Allah not profit your business.","title":"Dua for the person who trades in the mosque","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 1321","reflection":"This masjid dua reminds Muslims to keep the mosque pure for Salah and zikr allah, teaching the right way to respect Allah’s house and keep business outside its doors.","lesson":"Masjid dua helps Muslims remember not to mix business with Salah and Amal."},{"id":187,"text":"O Allah! separate me from my sins as You have separated the East from the West. O Allah, cleanse me of my transgressions as the white garment is cleansed of stains. O Allah! wash away my sins with ice and water and frost.","title":"Dua after Takbeer in Salah","source":"Bukhari: 744","reflection":"This dua after takbeer in salah helps a Muslim start prayer with a clean heart, asking Allah to keep sins far away and make every namaz pure and full of Barakah and forgiveness.","lesson":"Allahumma baid in dua al istiftah keeps sins far like east and west in namaz."},{"id":188,"text":"O Allah, Lord of Jibra-eel, Meeka-eel and Israfeel (great angles), Creator of the heavens and the Earth, Knower of the seen and the unseen. You are the arbitrator between Your servants in that which they have disputed. Guide me to the truth by Your leave, in that which they have differed, for verily You guide whom You will to a straight path.","title":"Dua When Starting Tahajjud Prayer","source":"Muslim: 770","reflection":"This dua for tahajjud prayer before salah brings a Muslim closer to Allah, filling the heart with Barakah and Iman, and helps guide to sirat al mustaqim in the quiet of night.","lesson":"Allah gives Barakah to the one who makes this dua for tahajjud prayer."},{"id":190,"text":"O Allah, You are the Sovereign, none has the right to be worshipped except You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant, I have wronged my own soul and have acknowledged my sin, so forgive me all my sins for no one forgives sins except You. Guide me to the best of characters for none can guide to it other than You, and deliver me from the worst of characters for none can deliver me from it other than You.","title":"Dua at Tahajjud (At Beginning)","source":"Muslim: 771","reflection":"This dua at tahajjud helps a muslim ask Allah for forgiveness and good character, making the night prayer more blessed and full of hope for those who seek Allah’s mercy and guidance.","lesson":"Allahumma in this dua at tahajjud brings true repentance in islam to the heart."},{"id":191,"text":"Here I am, in answer to Your call, happy to serve you. All good is within Your hands and evil does not stem from You. I exist by your will and will return to you. Blessed and High are You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent unto You.","title":"Dua at the start of the prayer (after takbeer)","source":"Muslim: 771","reflection":"This dua before salat after takbeer reminds a muslim to start salah with a clean heart, seeking Allah’s forgiveness and Barakah before every prayer for better Amal and Iman.","lesson":"Dua before salat helps muslims begin salah with istighfar and pure niyyah."},{"id":192,"text":"Allah is the Greatest, Most Great. Allah is the Greatest, Most Great. Allah is the Greatest, Most Great. Praise is to Allah, abundantly. Praise is to Allah, abundantly. Praise is to Allah, abundantly. Glory is to Allah, at the break of day and at its end.","title":"Dua at the Beginning of Salah (Allahu Akbar Kabira)","source":"Hasan li gairihi (Shu'aib Al-Arnaut). Abu Dawud: 764","reflection":"This before namaz dua with allahu akbar kabira fills the heart with praise and thanks, helping a muslim start salah with strong Iman and Barakah from the first takbeer to the last.","lesson":"Allahu akbar in dua before salah lifts the heart with praise and true tawheed."},{"id":195,"text":"Glory to my Lord the Exalted.","title":"Dua in Ruku (Subhana Rabbiyal Azeem)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 262","reflection":"This dua in ruku brings a muslim closer to Allah, showing respect and praise, and helps keep the heart humble during every step of salah and muslim prayer.","lesson":"Subhana rabbiyal azeem in ruku shows true respect for Allah’s greatness."},{"id":196,"text":"Glory and praise be to my mighty Lord.","title":"Dua For Ruku (Subhana Rabbiyal Adheem Wa Bihamdihi)","source":"Hasan Sanad (Shu'aib Al-Arnaut). Abu Dawud: 870","reflection":"This dua for ruku helps a muslim praise Allah with both words and heart, making every ruku in salah more meaningful and full of Barakah for those who follow the sunnah.","lesson":"Subhana rabbiyal azeem wa bihamdihi in ruku brings double reward and praise."},{"id":197,"text":"Glory (to You), Most Holy (are You), Lord of the angels and the Spirit.","title":"Dua in Ruku (Subbuhun Quddusun Rabbul Mala Ikati War Ruh)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 872","reflection":"This ruku dua helps a muslim praise Allah as the Lord of angels and the Spirit, making every ruku in salah more special and full of respect for Allah’s greatness.","lesson":"Subbuhun quddusun in ruku shows deep respect for Allah’s pure and holy names."},{"id":198,"text":"O Allah, to You I bow (in prayer) and in You I believe and to You I have submitted. Before You my hearing is humbled, as is my sight, my mind, my bones, my nerves.","title":"Dua For Ruku (Allahumma Laka Rakatu Wa Bika Amantu)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 760","reflection":"This dua for ruku helps a muslim show full trust and surrender to Allah, making every ruku in salah a time of true belief and respect for the Creator in every part of the body.","lesson":"Allahumma laka rakatu in ruku shows full Amal and trust in Allah’s power."},{"id":199,"text":"Glory is to You, Master of power, of dominion, of majesty and greatness.","title":"Dua at Ruku","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 873","reflection":"This dua in ruku helps a Muslim praise Allah’s power and greatness, making every ruku in salah a time to remember Allah’s control over all things and His high status.","lesson":"Subhaana dhil-jabarooti in ruku shows true praise for Allah’s power and rule."},{"id":200,"text":"Glory is to You O Allah, and praise. I ask you for forgiveness and I turn to you (from sinning).","title":"Dua in Rukoo (Subhanaka wa Bihamdika Astaghfiruka)","source":"Hasan (Albani). Silsila Sahiha: 3032","reflection":"This ruku dua brings a Muslim closer to Allah’s mercy and forgiveness, making every ruku in Salah a time for praise, repentance, and seeking Barakah from the Most Forgiving.","lesson":"Allah forgives sins when a Muslim says ruku dua with a heart full of Iman."},{"id":201,"text":"Glory is to You, O Allah, our Lord, and praise is Yours. O Allah, forgive me. [1]","title":"Dua in Ruku (Dua for forgiveness)","source":"[1] Bukhari: 794 [2] Sura Nasr 110:3","reflection":"This dua in ruku brings a Muslim closer to Allah’s mercy and forgiveness, helping hearts stay humble and pure while bowing in Salah and asking for Allah’s kindness and Barakah in every prayer.","lesson":"Allah’s mercy comes close when a Muslim says subhanakallahumma in ruku."},{"id":202,"text":"Allah hears whoever praises Him.","title":"Dua After Ruku (Sami Allahu Liman Hamidah)","source":"Bukhari: 796","reflection":"This dua after ruku reminds Muslims that Allah listens to every word of praise, making Salah more meaningful and filling the heart with thankfulness and hope for Allah’s Barakah and kindness.","lesson":"Allah listens to the one who says sami allahu liman hamidah after ruku."},{"id":203,"text":"O Allah, our Rabb (Lord), to You is praise in all the heavens and all the earth, and all that You Will (to create) afterwards, O You, Who are worthy of praise and glory, the most worthy of what a slave says - and we are all Your slaves: no one can withhold what You give, or give what You withhold, and riches cannot avail a wealthy person against You.","title":"Dua After Ruku (Allahumma Rabbana Wa Lakal-Hamd)","source":"Muslim: 477","reflection":"This dua after ruku fills the heart with praise for Allah, reminding Muslims that all power and gifts come from Him alone, and brings Barakah and thankfulness in every Salah and daily Amal.","lesson":"Allah’s gifts and Barakah reach the one who says rabbana lakal hamd after ruku."},{"id":204,"text":"[1] Our Lord, to You be the praise. [2] O Allah, our Lord, to You be the praise.","title":"Rabbana Lakal Hamd (Dua After Ruku)","source":"Bukhari: 796","reflection":"This short dua after ruku fills Salah with thankfulness, helping Muslims remember Allah’s gifts and making every prayer more full of Barakah and Iman for those who say it with a true heart.","lesson":"Allah’s praise grows in the heart when a Muslim says rabbana lakal hamd after ruku."},{"id":205,"text":"[1] Our Lord and to You be the praise. [2] O Allah, our Lord and to You be the praise.","title":"Rabbana Wa Lakal Hamd (Dua After Rukoo)","source":"Bukhari: 795","reflection":"This dua after rukoo helps Muslims show thankfulness to Allah in Salah, making every prayer more full of Barakah and reminding hearts to praise Allah for all His gifts and kindness in daily life.","lesson":"Allah’s Barakah comes to the one who says rabbana wa lakal hamd after rukoo."},{"id":207,"text":"Praise be to You, O Allah, our Lord! Praise be to You, it fills the heavens, fills the earth, completes all that is in between them, and then it completes whatever You will.","title":"Dua After Raising from Ruku","source":"Muslim: 476","reflection":"This dua after ruku fills your heart with praise for Allah, making your salah more complete and bringing more blessings every time you stand up from bowing in prayer.","lesson":"Allahumma rabbana dua after ruku brings more Barakah in every Muslim prayer."},{"id":208,"text":"Allah! our Lord, to Thee be the praise that would fill the heavens and the earth and that which is between them, and that which will please Thee besides (them). Worthy art Thou of all praise and glory. No one can withhold what Thou givest, or give what Thou withholdest. And the greatness O! the great availeth not against Thee.","title":"Dua When Raising From Ruku #2","source":"Muslim: 478","reflection":"This dua after ruku reminds us that only Allah gives and takes, filling our prayers with praise and trust, and making every Muslim prayer more blessed and accepted by Allah.","lesson":"Allahumma rabbana dua after ruku shows full trust in Allah’s power and gifts."},{"id":209,"text":"Praise be to Allah, much good and blessed praise as our Lord loves and is pleased with","title":"Dua Praising Allah (Dua After Ruku)","source":"Hasan (Albani). Sunan Nasai: 931","reflection":"This after ruku dua fills your prayer with words that Allah loves, bringing more Barakah and making your salah steps more pleasing to Him every time you praise Him in namaz.","lesson":"Alhamdu lillahi after ruku dua brings praise that Allah loves and accepts."},{"id":213,"text":"Glory is to my Lord, the Most High.","title":"Dua in Sujood (Subhana Rabbiyal Ala)","source":"Muslim: 772","reflection":"This dua in sujood brings you closer to Allah, filling your sajdah with praise and making your salah more loved by Allah every time you say subhana rabbiyal ala in prayer.","lesson":"Subhana rabbiyal ala in sujood brings more Barakah and peace in every sajdah."},{"id":214,"text":"Glory and praise be to my most high Lord.","title":"Dua for Sajdah (Sajda Dua)","source":"Hasan Sanad (Shu'aib Al-Arnaut). Abu Dawud: 870","reflection":"Feel the closeness to Allah and raise your Iman by saying sajda dua in every sujood, as this short prayer brings blessings and peace to the heart of every Muslim.","lesson":"Subhana rabbiyal ala in sujood brings Barakah and makes Salah more accepted."},{"id":215,"text":"O Allah, forgive me all my sins, great and small, the first and the last, those that are apparent and those that are hidden.","title":"Dua for Sujood (Allahumma Maghfir Lee)","source":"Muslim: 483","reflection":"Ask Allah for full forgiveness in every sujood with this powerful dua, letting your heart find peace and hope while you pray for mercy and a clean record of deeds.","lesson":"Allahummaghfirli zambi in sujood helps wipe away all types of sins for Muslims."},{"id":216,"text":"O Allah, I seek protection in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek protection in Your forgiveness from Your punishment. I seek protection in You from You. I cannot count Your praises. You are as You have praised Yourself.","title":"Dua After Ruku (Supplication Upon Rising From Bowing)","source":"Muslim:486, Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3566","reflection":"Find peace and hope by saying this dua after ruku, as it brings Allah’s mercy, keeps the heart humble, and helps every Muslim stay safe from anger and punishment.","lesson":"Allahumma inni in ruku dua brings Allah’s pleasure and keeps away His anger."},{"id":217,"text":"O Allah, place light in my heart, and in my ears light and in my sight light, and to my right light, and to my left light, and before me light and behind me light, and above me light, and below me light. O Allah, Make for me light, and make me a light, and place in my soul light, and place light in my nerves, and in my flesh light and in my blood light and in my hair light and in my skin light. O Allah, grant me light.","title":"Dua When Raising From Ruku (Dua Noor)","source":"Sahih Bukhari: 6316, Sahih Muslim: 763","reflection":"Ask Allah for noor in every part of life with this dua after ruku, letting your heart and actions shine bright with His light and guidance in every step you take.","lesson":"Dua for light fills the heart and face with noor and brings peace in Amal."},{"id":219,"text":"Glory (to You), Most Holy (are You), Lord of the angels and the Spirit.","title":"Dua in Sujood (Subbuhun Quddusun Rabbul Mala Ikati War Ruh)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 872","reflection":"This dua in sujood brings a Muslim closer to Allah, filling the heart with peace and reminding us of His greatness and mercy during the most humble part of salah.","lesson":"Allah’s mercy comes close when a Muslim says subbuhun quddusun in sujood."},{"id":220,"text":"O Allah, to You I prostrate myselfm, to You I have submitted, and in You I believe. My face is prostrated to the One Who created it, fashioned it, and gave it hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah, the Best of creators.","title":"Dua in Sujood (Allaahumma Laka Sajadtu wa Laka Aslamtu)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Nasai: 1126","reflection":"This dua for sujood helps a Muslim show full trust in Allah, making every prostration in salah more meaningful and filling the heart with thankfulness for His gifts and mercy.","lesson":"Allahumma in sujood shows a Muslim’s full Amal and trust in Allah’s plan."},{"id":221,"text":"Glory is to You, Master of power, of dominion, of majesty and greatness.","title":"Dua for Sujood","source":"Hasan (Albani). Abu Dawud: 873","reflection":"This dua for sujood reminds Muslims of Allah’s greatness and power, making every prostration in salah more deep and helping hearts feel close to the Master of all things.","lesson":"Saying this dua in sujood helps Muslims remember Allah’s full power and control."},{"id":222,"text":"O My Lord, forgive me. My Lord, forgive me.","title":"Dua between two Sujood","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 874","reflection":"This dua between two sujood helps a muslim ask Allah for forgiveness, making salah more soft and filling the heart with hope for mercy and a clean record of deeds.","lesson":"Rabbighfirli dua brings Allah’s forgiveness close and wipes away small sins."},{"id":223,"text":"O Allah! Pardon me, have mercy on me, guide me, and grant me sustenance.","title":"Dua between Sujood (Allahummaghfirli Warhamni Wahdini Warzuqni)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 284, Hasan (Albani). Abu Dawud: 850","reflection":"This dua between two sujood helps a muslim ask Allah for forgiveness, mercy, health, guidance, and rizq, making every salah more full of hope and Barakah from Allah.","lesson":"Allahummaghfirli dua brings Allah’s maghfirat and covers the heart with His mercy."},{"id":225,"text":"O Allah, write it as a reward for me, and release me from a sin for it, and make it a treasure for me in Paradise. Accept it from me as You accepted it from your servant Dawud.","title":"Dua For Sajdah in Quran","source":"Hasan (Albani). Tirmidhi: 579","reflection":"This dua for sujood after ayat sajadah in Quran brings reward, removes sins, and helps a Muslim gain closeness to Allah, making every sajdah in tilawat e quran more meaningful and accepted.","lesson":"Allah gives reward for every sajdah in quran recitation with this dua for sujood."},{"id":226,"text":"I have prostrated my face to the One Who created it, and gave it hearing and sight by His might and His power.","title":"Sajdah Dua for night recitation","source":"Hasan (Albani). Tirmidhi: 580","reflection":"This sajdah dua for sujood in tahajjud prayer helps a Muslim remember Allah’s power, brings forgiveness, and makes night prayer more special with true Iman and Barakah in every prostration.","lesson":"Allah’s might is remembered when muslims use this dua for sujood in tahajjud."},{"id":227,"text":"I have prostrated my face to the One Who created it, and gave it hearing and sight by His might and His power. So blessed is Allah, the best of creators.","title":"Dua after Reciting the Verses of Prostration","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3425, Sura Al Muminun 23:14","reflection":"This sujood dua after sajdah tilawat in quran recitation praises Allah as the best creator, brings Barakah, and helps a Muslim remember His power and mercy in every sajda after reading quran.","lesson":"Allah’s greatness is praised with this sujood dua from surah al muminun in quran."},{"id":228,"text":"All greetings of humility are for Allah, and all prayers and goodness. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous slaves of Allah. I bear witness that there is none worthy of worship but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and His Messenger.","title":"Tashahhud Dua (Attahiyat Lillahi Wa Salawatu)","source":"Bukhari: 7381","reflection":"This tashahhud dua in salah brings peace, affirms faith, and connects a Muslim with Allah and His Prophet, making every attahiyat in namaz full of Barakah and acceptance.","lesson":"Attahiyat lillahi wa salawatu affirms the oneness of Allah and true Iman."},{"id":229,"text":"O Allah, bestow Your favor on Muhammad (ﷺ) and on the family of Muhammad as You have bestowed Your favor on Ibrahim and on the family of Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Most Glorious. O Allah, bless Muhammad (ﷺ) and the family of Muhammad as You have blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Most Glorious.","title":"Durood Sharif (Durood Ibrahim)","source":"Bukhari: 3370","reflection":"Durood Ibrahim brings blessings and mercy for Prophet Muhammad and his family, increases Barakah in a Muslim’s life, and is a special dua after tashahhud in every salah for acceptance and reward.","lesson":"Allahumma salli ala muhammad brings Allah’s mercy on Prophet and his family."},{"id":230,"text":"O Allah, bestow Your favor on Muhammad (ﷺ) and upon his wives and progeny as You have bestowed Your favor upon the family of Ibrahim. And bless Muhammad (ﷺ) and his wives and progeny as You have blessed the family of Ibrahim, You are full of praise, Most Glorious.","title":"Dua after Tashahhud (Darood Sharif)","source":"Bukhari: 3369","reflection":"This dua after attahiyat brings blessings and peace, connecting hearts to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ and his family, and brings Allah’s mercy for those who recite it in their Salah every day.","lesson":"Allahumma salli ala Muhammad brings Barakah and Rahmah in a muslim’s namaz."},{"id":231,"text":"O Allah, join our hearts, mend our social relationship, guide us to the path of peace, bring us from darkness to light, save us from obscenities, outward or inward, and bless our ears, our eyes, our hearts, our wives, our children, and relent toward us; Thou art the Relenting, the Merciful. And make us grateful for Thy blessing and make us praise it while accepting it and give it to us in full.","title":"Dua Masura #1 (Allahumma Allif Baina Qulubina)","source":"Daif (Albani). Abu Dawud: 969","reflection":"This dua e masura brings hearts together, helps families and friends stay close, and asks Allah for peace, light, and Barakah in every part of a muslim’s life, both inside and out.","lesson":"Allahumma Allif Baina Qulubina keeps love and unity strong in muslim families."},{"id":232,"text":"O Allah! I seek refuge with Thee from the torment of the Hell, from the torment of the grave, from the trial of life and death and from the evil of the trial of Masih al-Dajjal.","title":"Dua e Masura #2 (Dua For Protection From Hellfire)","source":"Muslim: 588","reflection":"This dua e masura in english asks Allah to keep muslims safe from Jahannam, the grave, and all big tests, making it a strong hifazat ki dua for every believer’s daily Amal and Iman.","lesson":"Dua for protection from evil keeps muslims safe from Jahannam’s punishment."},{"id":233,"text":"O Allah, forgive me what I have sent before me and what I have left behind me, what I have concealed and what I have done openly, what I have done in excess, and what You are better aware of than I. You are the One Who sends forth and You are the One Who delays. There is none worthy of worship but You.","title":"Dua Masura #3 (Allahummaghfirli Ma Qaddamtu)","source":"Muslim: 771","reflection":"This dua e masura for forgiveness helps Muslims ask Allah to clean all sins, hidden or open, and brings hope for maghfirat and mercy in every Muslim’s Amal and daily Salah.","lesson":"Allahummaghfirli Ma Qaddamtu wipes away old and new sins from a Muslim’s life."},{"id":234,"text":"O Allah, I have greatly wronged myself and no one forgives sins but You. So, grant me forgiveness and have mercy on me. Surely, you are Forgiving, Merciful.","title":"Dua e Masura #4 (Allahumma Inni Zalamtu Nafsi)","source":"Bukhari: 834","reflection":"This dua e masura in namaz helps Muslims admit their mistakes and ask Allah for His maghfirat and Rahmah, making hearts soft and bringing hope for forgiveness in every Salah.","lesson":"Allahumma inni zalamtu nafsi brings Allah’s maghfirat for big and small sins."},{"id":236,"text":"O Allah, I ask You for all that is good, in this world and in the Hereafter, what I know and what I do not know. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from all evil, in this world and in the Hereafter, what I know and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the good that Your slave and Prophet (ﷺ) has asked You for, and I seek refuge with You from the evil from which Your slave and Prophet (ﷺ) sought refuge. O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and for that which brings one closer to it, in word and deed, and I seek refuge in You from Hell and from that which brings one closer to it, in word and deed. And I ask You to make every decree that You decree concerning me good.","title":"Dua Masurah #6 (Allahumma Inni As Aluka Min Khairi)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Ibn Majah: 3846","reflection":"This dua e masura helps a Muslim ask Allah for every good thing and safety from all harm, making the heart strong in Amal and bringing hope for Jannah and Barakah in every part of life.","lesson":"Allah gives a Muslim Barakah and keeps away all evil with dua masura."},{"id":237,"text":"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the False Messiah, and I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from sin and from debt.","title":"Dua For Protection From Punishment Of Grave, Hell And Dajjal","source":"Bukhari: 832","reflection":"This dua e masura keeps a Muslim safe from the hardest trials and brings Allah’s help in every part of life, asking for Barakah, forgiveness, and protection from all evil and fitna.","lesson":"Allah keeps a Muslim safe from grave’s punishment with this dua for protection."},{"id":238,"text":"O Allah, I seek refuge with Thee from the torment of Hell, and I seek refuge with Thee from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge with Thee from the trial of the Masih al-Dajjal (Antichrist) and I seek refuge with Thee from the trial of life and death. O Allah! I seek refuge with Thee from sin and debt.","title":"Dua at the end of Salah (Allahumma Inni A Uzu Bika)","source":"Muslim: 1/412","reflection":"This dua e masura helps a Muslim find Allah’s protection from every big trial, keeping the heart safe from Jahannam, Dajjal, and the burden of sins and debt after every Salah.","lesson":"Allah saves a Muslim from Jahannam’s azaab with this dua after salah."},{"id":239,"text":"O Allah, help me to remember You, to give You thanks, and to perform Your worship in the best manner.","title":"Dua Masoora #7 (Allahumma A Inni Ala Zikrika)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1522","reflection":"This dua e masura helps a Muslim keep Allah close in every Amal, making the heart full of shukr, strong in zikrullah, and always ready for good ibadah after every prayer.","lesson":"Allah gives a Muslim power for zikrullah and keeps the heart soft with this dua."},{"id":240,"text":"O Allah! I seek refuge with You from cowardice, and miserliness, and seek refuge with You from reaching a degraded helpless old age, and seek refuge with You from the afflictions of the world and from the punishment in the grave.","title":"Dua Masoorah #8 (Allahumma Inni A Uzu Bika Minal)","source":"Bukhari: 6374","reflection":"This dua e masura helps a Muslim stay safe from the bad things of dunya, asking Allah for Barakah, courage, and protection from grave’s azaab and every fitna in life.","lesson":"Allah keeps a Muslim away from bukhil and gives Barakah with this protection dua."},{"id":241,"text":"O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and seek Your protection from the Fire.","title":"Dua For Jannah (Allahumma Inni As Aluka Al Jannah)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Ibn Majah 3846","reflection":"This dua for jannah helps a Muslim ask Allah for the best place in akhirah, keeping the heart full of hope, Barakah, and safety from Jahannam in every part of life.","lesson":"Allah gives a Muslim hope for Jannah Firdaus with this simple dua for jannah."},{"id":242,"text":"O Allah, I ask You. O Allah, You are the One, the Only, Self-Sufficient Master, Who was not begotten and begets not and none is equal to Him. Forgive me my sins, surely you are Forgiving, Merciful.","title":"Dua Masura #9 (Allahumma Inni As Aluka Ya Allah Bi'Annaka)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Nasai: 1301","reflection":"This dua masura helps a Muslim ask Allah for forgiveness by calling Him with His special names, bringing Barakah, mercy, and hope for maghfirat in every part of life.","lesson":"Allah forgives sins and gives maghfirat with this dua e masura after salah."},{"id":243,"text":"O Allah, I ask You as unto You is all praise, none has the right to be worshipped except You, alone, without partner. You are the Benefactor. Originator of the heavens and the Earth, O Possessor of majesty and honour, O Ever Living, O Self-Subsisting and Supporter of all. I am asking you","title":"Dua Masura #10","source":"Sahih (Albani). Nasai: 1300","reflection":"This dua e masura helps a muslim call Allah with His most beautiful names, bringing Barakah, hope, and strength in every Amal by praising Him as Ya Hayyu Ya Qayyum and Ya Dhal Jalali wal Ikram.","lesson":"Allah gives Barakah and answers dua when called with ya hayyu ya qayyum."},{"id":244,"text":"O Allah, I ask You, by the fact that I bear witness that You are Allah. There is none worthy of worship but You, the Only ilah, Independent of creation, Who was not begotten and begets not, and none is equal to Him.","title":"Dua e Masura #11 (Allahumma Inni As Aluka Bi Annaka Antallah Full Dua)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1493","reflection":"This dua e masura helps a muslim call Allah by His special names, bringing Barakah, strong Iman, and hope for every Amal by remembering He is Al Ahad, Allahu Samad, and there is no one like Him.","lesson":"Allah answers dua when a muslim calls Him with la ilaha illa anta and allahumma."},{"id":245,"text":"O Allah, I ask You, as You are the Owner of praise, there is none worthy of worship but You alone, You have no partner. You are the Giver of all good. O Creator of the heavens and the earth, Owner of majesty and honor. O Living and Everlasting One, I ask you for Paradise and I seek refuge in You from the fire.","title":"Dua E Masurah #12","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1493-1495","reflection":"This beautiful dua e masurah asks Allah for Jannah and protection from Jahannam, using His blessed names like ya hayyu ya qayyum and ya dhal jalali wal ikram, bringing hope and peace to every muslim heart.","lesson":"Allah grants Jannah to the muslim who makes this dua e masurah with Iman."},{"id":246,"text":"Allah is the Greatest, Most Great. Praise is to Allah, abundantly. Glory is to Allah, at the break of day and at its end.","title":"Dua in Salah (Allahu Akbar Kabira Walhamdulillah Kaseera)","source":"Muslim: 601","reflection":"This dua for salah fills the heart with Allah’s greatness and praise, making every muslim’s namaz start with Barakah and peace, and helps keep the mind focused on Allah from start to end.","lesson":"Allahu akbar kabira in dua istiftah lifts the heart with Allah’s greatness in salah."},{"id":247,"text":"O Allah, I ask You for knowledge which is beneficial and sustenance which is good, and deeds which are acceptable.","title":"Dua After Fajr Prayer (Allahumma Inni As Aluka Ilman)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Ibn Majah: 925","reflection":"This dua after fajr prayer brings a muslim closer to Allah’s mercy, asking for good knowledge, pure rizq, and accepted Amal, making every morning start with hope and Barakah from fajr namaz.","lesson":"Allahumma inni as aluka ilman in fajr dua brings useful knowledge for muslims."},{"id":248,"text":"None has the right to be worshipped except Allah, who is alone and does not have any partner. To Him belongs all sovereignty and praise, He gives life and causes death and He is omnipotent over all things.","title":"Dua After Fajr and Maghrib #1","source":"Hasan (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3534","reflection":"This dua after fajr prayer and maghrib reminds every muslim of Allah’s oneness, power, and mercy, making the heart strong with shahada and filling the day and night with Barakah and peace.","lesson":"La ilaha illallahu in this dua after fajr prayer keeps Iman strong and pure."},{"id":249,"text":"O Allah, protect me from Hell.","title":"Dua After Fajr and Maghrib #2 (Allahumma Ajirni Minan Naar)","source":"Hasan (Ibn Hajar). Al-futuhaatur Rabbaniyyah 3/69","reflection":"This dua after maghrib prayer and fajr asks Allah for protection from Jahannam, making every muslim’s morning and evening full of hope, safety, and Allah’s mercy in daily life.","lesson":"Allahumma ajirni minan naar in maghrib dua keeps muslim safe from Jahannam."},{"id":250,"text":"I ask Allah for forgiveness.","title":"Dua After Salah (Astaghfirullah)","source":"Sahih Muslim: 591","reflection":"Astaghfirullah after salah helps every muslim seek Allah’s forgiveness, making the heart clean and bringing Barakah to daily Amal, while keeping the soul close to Allah’s mercy and kindness.","lesson":"Astaghfirullah after salah wipes away small sins and mistakes from Amal."},{"id":251,"text":"O Allah, You are Peace and from You comes peace. Blessed are You, O Owner of majesty and honor.","title":"Dua After Salat (Allahumma Antas Salam Wa Minkas Salam Dua)","source":"Muslim: 591","reflection":"This dua after salat fills the heart with peace from Allah, reminding every muslim that true safety and Barakah come only from Him, and brings honor by calling ya zal jalali wal ikram after every namaz.","lesson":"Allahumma antas salam in dua after prayer brings real peace to muslim heart."},{"id":252,"text":"None has the right to be worshipped except Allah, alone, without partner, to Him belongs all sovereignty and praise and and He is Able to do all things. O Allah, none can prevent what You have willed to bestow and none can bestow what You have willed to prevent, and no wealth or majesty can benefit anyone, as from You is all wealth and majesty.","title":"Dua After Salam","source":"Bukhari: 844","reflection":"This dua after salam reminds every muslim that all power and gifts come from Allah alone, making the heart strong in Tawheed and filling daily life with Barakah, hope, and trust in Allah’s plan.","lesson":"La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu in dua after salam keeps Iman pure."},{"id":253,"text":"None has the right to be worshipped except Allah, alone, without partner, to Him belongs all sovereignty and praise and and He is Able to do all things, there is no might nor power except with Allah. None has the right to be worshipped except Allah and we worship none except Him. For Him is all favor, grace, and glorious praise. None has the right to be worshipped except Allah and we are sincere in faith and devotion to Him although the disbelievers detest it.","title":"Dua After Salam in Prayer","source":"Muslim: 594","reflection":"This dua after salam in prayer fills the heart with Tawheed, trust, and pure Iman, reminding every Muslim that all power, praise, and blessings come only from Allah, and keeps the soul safe with daily zikr.","lesson":"La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu in dua after prayer keeps faith strong."},{"id":257,"text":"How perfect Allah is, all praise is for Allah, and Allah is the greatest.","title":"Powerful dhikr after salah","source":"Muslim 1/418, no.597","reflection":"This dhikr after salah fills the heart with peace and brings Allah’s mercy close, making every Muslim feel the blessings of subhanallah alhamdulillah allahu akbar in daily life.","lesson":"Subhanallah and alhamdulillah with allahu akbar make Iman strong after every salah."},{"id":258,"text":"O Allah, save me from Your punishment on the Day when You resurrect - or gather - Your slaves.","title":"Dua at end of Salah","source":"Muslim: 709","reflection":"This dua at end of salah asks Allah for safety from His punishment and brings hope to every Muslim who wants forgiveness and mercy on the Day when all people will stand before Him.","lesson":"Allah’s mercy comes close for the Muslim who makes dua after salah with yaqeen."},{"id":259,"text":"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from Kufr, poverty, and from the torment of the grave.","title":"Dua at the end of Salah","source":"Sahih (Albani). Nasai: 5465","reflection":"This dua at the end of salah asks Allah for protection from kufr, poverty, and the pain of the grave, giving every Muslim hope for safety and peace in this world and the next.","lesson":"Allahumma inni auzubika keeps a Muslim safe from kufr and weak Iman after salah."},{"id":260,"text":"O Allah, help me to remember You, to give You thanks, and to perform Your worship in the best manner.","title":"Dua After Salah (Allahumma a inni ala zikrika wa shukrika)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1522","reflection":"This dua after salah asks Allah for help in remembering Him, giving thanks, and doing ibadah in the best way, making every Muslim’s heart full of zikr and shukr after every prayer.","lesson":"Allahumma a inni ala zikrika wa shukrika brings Barakah in every Muslim’s amal."},{"id":261,"text":"O Allah, forgive me what I have sent before me and what I have left behind me, what I have done in secret and what I have done in public, what I have done in excess, and those sins which You are better aware of than I. You are the One Who sends forth and You are the One Who delays. There is none worthy of worship but You.","title":"Dua After Namaz","source":"[1] Muslim: 771 [2] Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1509","reflection":"This dua after namaz asks Allah to forgive every sin, hidden or open, and brings hope for mercy to every Muslim who wants a clean heart and Allah’s forgiveness after every salah.","lesson":"Allahummaghfirli ma qaddamtu helps a Muslim get forgiveness for all past mistakes."},{"id":262,"text":"O Allah, set straight my religious commitment that You have made a protection for me, and set straight my worldly affairs which You have made a means of my livelihood. O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. O Allah, None can withhold what you have given and none can give what you have withheld, and no wealth or fortune can avail the man of wealth and fortune before You.","title":"Dua at the end of Namaz","source":"Hasan (Ibn Hajar). Alfutuhatur Rabbaniyyah 3/71","reflection":"This dua at the end of namaz asks Allah to fix both deen and dunya, bringing His mercy and help to every Muslim who wants a good life and strong Iman after every salah.","lesson":"Allahumma la mania lima ataita keeps rizq safe and brings Barakah in daily life."},{"id":263,"text":"Ya Allah! I try by your help, fight by your help, show courage by your help and be victorious by your help.","title":"Dua After Prayer","source":"Sahih (Albani). Darimi: 2/217","reflection":"This dua after prayer asks Allah for help in every struggle, making a muslim strong and brave with His support in every part of life after every salah.","lesson":"Allahumma gives a muslim strength to face mushkil and win with Allah’s help."},{"id":264,"text":"O Allah, forgive me and turn to me. You are the Ever-Turning, the Merciful' (in another narration: the Most Forgiving)","title":"Dua After Salat (Allahummaghfirli Warhamni Wa Tub Alayya)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Sahihah: 556, Ahmad: 5564","reflection":"This dua after salat asks Allah for forgiveness and mercy, helping every muslim find hope and a clean heart after every prayer by trusting in Allah’s kindness and His power to accept tawbah.","lesson":"Allahummaghfirli warhamni brings Allah’s mercy and wipes away old sins after salat."},{"id":265,"text":"Ya Allah! Forgive all of my mistakes and my sins. Ya Allah! Inspire me and make me obedient. Guide me to do the good deeds and to the good mannars. Because none can guide to it’s good and turn away from it except you.","title":"Dua for After Namaz","source":"Hasan (Albani). Sahih Al Jame: 1266","reflection":"This dua for after namaz helps a muslim ask Allah for forgiveness and good manners, making every salah a time to seek His mercy and guidance for better actions and a clean heart.","lesson":"Allahumma in this dua after namaz brings forgiveness for all mistakes and sins."},{"id":266,"text":"O Allah, forgive me my sin, and expand for me my abode, and bless for me that which You have provided me.","title":"Dua for After Salah","source":"Hasan (Albani). Sahih Al Jame: 1265","reflection":"This dua for after salah helps a muslim ask Allah for forgiveness, Barakah in rizq, and a peaceful home, making every prayer a time to seek His mercy and blessings for daily life and family.","lesson":"Allahumma in this dua after salah brings Allah’s forgiveness for every sin."},{"id":267,"text":"Allah is the greatest.","title":"Dhikr After Salah","source":"Bukhari: 842","reflection":"Saying Allahu Akbar after salah reminds a muslim that Allah is the greatest, bringing peace to the heart and making every prayer more strong with the power of takbir and true Iman.","lesson":"Takbir after salah lifts the heart and keeps Allah’s greatness in the mind."},{"id":268,"text":"Glory is to Allah and praise is to Him, by the multitude of His creation, by His Pleasure, by the weight of His Throne, and by the extent of His Words.","title":"Namaz After Dua","source":"Muslim: 2726","reflection":"Saying subhanallahi wa bihamdihi after namaz fills the heart with praise for Allah, making every prayer more strong and bringing His pleasure, mercy, and blessings in daily life.","lesson":"Subhanallahi wa bihamdihi in tasbih after namaz brings Allah’s pleasure and mercy."},{"id":273,"text":"Glory is to You O Allah, and praise. Blessed is Your Name and Exalted is Your Majesty. There is none worthy of worship but You.","title":"Dua For Starting Tahajjud Prayer (Subhanaka Allahumma)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 775","reflection":"This dua for starting tahajjud prayer fills the heart with Allah’s praise, making the night prayer more strong and bringing Barakah, mercy, and closeness to Allah in every tahajjud.","lesson":"Subhanaka Allahumma in tahajjud prayer brings Allah’s Barakah and mercy."},{"id":274,"text":"Glory is to the King, the Holy.","title":"Dua After Witr Prayer (Subhanal Malikil Quddus)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud No. 1430; An-Nasa'i No. 1699, 1701","reflection":"Saying subhanal malikil quddus after witr prayer fills the heart with Allah’s greatness, making the end of night prayer special and bringing peace, Barakah, and purity to every muslim.","lesson":"Subhanal malikil quddus in dua after witr prayer brings Allah’s purity and praise."},{"id":275,"text":"O Allah, I seek refuge with Your Pleasure from Your anger. I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment. I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot count Your praises, You are as You have praised Yourself.","title":"Dua after Witr Namaz (Allahumma Inni a'uzu Bi Ridaka)","source":"Sahih. Abu Dawud: 1427","reflection":"This dua after witr namaz helps a muslim seek Allah’s pleasure and forgiveness, making the end of night prayer a time for protection, mercy, and true praise to Allah.","lesson":"Dua after witr namaz asks Allah for protection from His anger and punishment."},{"id":276,"text":"Lord of the angels and the Spirit.","title":"Dua after witr salah (Rabbul-mala'ikati war ruh)","source":"Sunan Daraqutni 2/31, Mu'jamul Awsat 8/108, Sunan Bayhaqi 3/40","reflection":"This dua after witr salah reminds a muslim of Allah’s power over all angels and Jibreel, making the end of night prayer full of praise, Barakah, and closeness to the Lord of the angels.","lesson":"Dua after witr salah with rabbul-mala'ikati war ruh shows Allah’s greatness."},{"id":278,"text":"O Allah, guide me with those whom You have guided, and strengthen me with those whom You have given strength. Take me to Your care with those whom You have taken to Your care. Bless me in what You have given me. Protect me from the evil You have ordained. Surely, You command and are not commanded, and none whom You have committed to Your care shall be humiliated and none whom You have taken as an enemy shall taste glory. You are Blessed, Our Lord, and Exalted.","title":"Dua for Witr (Doa Qunut)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1425","reflection":"Dua for witr, known as dua e qunoot, brings Allah’s guidance, protection, and Barakah, making the night prayer strong and filling the heart with hope, safety, and true blessings from Allah.","lesson":"Dua for witr asks Allah for hidayah and keeps a muslim on the right path."},{"id":279,"text":"My Lord, aid me and do not aid against me, and grant me victory and do not grant victory over me, plot for me and do not plot against me, guide me and facilitate guidance for me, grant me victory over those who transgress against me. My Lord, make me ever-grateful to You, ever-remembering of You, ever-fearful of You, ever-obedient to You, ever-humble to You, oft-turning and returning to You. My Lord, accept my repentance, wash my sin, answer my call, make firm my proof, make firm my tongue, guide my heart, and remove resentment from my heart (the treachery of my chest).","title":"Dua e qunoot (Rabbi A'inni Wala Tu'in 'Alayya)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Tirmidhi: 3551","reflection":"This dua e qunoot brings a muslim closer to Allah’s help and mercy, asking for strength, guidance, and forgiveness in every part of life, especially in times of need and hardship.","lesson":"Allah gives strength and help to the one who makes dua e qunoot with Iman."},{"id":280,"text":"O Allah, You alone do we worship and to You we pray and bow down prostrate. To You we hasten to worship and to serve. Our hope is for Your mercy and we fear Your punishment. Surely, Your punishment of the disbelievers is at hand. O Allah, we seek Your help and Your forgiveness, and we praise You beneficently. We do not deny You and we believe in You. We surrender to You and renounce whoever disbelieves in You.","title":"Dua Qunut (Allahumma inna nasta inuka)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Irwaul Galil: 2/170, Bayhaqi: As-Sunanul Kabra - 2/211","reflection":"This dua qunoot in witr prayer helps a muslim show true faith, ask for Allah’s mercy, and seek forgiveness, making the heart soft and full of hope in every salah and hardship.","lesson":"Allahumma inna nasta inuka brings Allah’s help and forgiveness in witr prayer."},{"id":282,"text":"Allah is the greatest.","title":"When waking up for Tahajjud prayer (Dhikr & Dua)","source":"Hasan (Albani). Abu Dawud: 766","reflection":"Saying Allahu Akbar before tahajjud prayer fills the heart with strength and helps a muslim remember Allah’s greatness in the quiet of night, making every tahajjud more special and full of Barakah.","lesson":"Allahu akbar before tahajjud brings the heart close to Allah’s greatness."},{"id":284,"text":"(135) And those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves [by transgression], remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins - and who can forgive sins except Allah ? - and [who] do not persist in what they have done while they know. (136) Those - their reward is forgiveness from their Lord and gardens beneath which rivers flow [in Paradise], wherein they will abide eternally; and excellent is the reward of the [righteous] workers. (Sura Ali Imran 3:135-136)","title":"Dua for Repentance after Sin (2 Rakat Prayer)","source":"Sahih (Albani). Abu Dawud: 1521","reflection":"This dua for repentance after sin helps a muslim turn back to Allah with a clean heart, seeking forgiveness and mercy, and brings hope for Jannah and a new start after every mistake.","lesson":"Dua for repentance brings Allah’s forgiveness and wipes away old sins fast."},{"id":285,"text":"O Allah, forgive him (person's name), raise his degree among those who are rightly guided, grant him a successor in his descendants who remain. Forgive us and him, O Lord of the Universe, and make his grave spacious, and grant him light in it.","title":"Dua for the deceased","source":"Muslim: 920","reflection":"This dua for the deceased brings hope and mercy for the one who passed away, asking Allah to forgive, give light in the grave, and raise their place among the guided with Barakah for their family.","lesson":"Dua for the deceased asks Allah to forgive and raise the person’s darajat."},{"id":287,"text":"With the Name of Allah and according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).","title":"Dua when placing the deceased in Grave","source":"Sahih. Abu Dawud: 3213","reflection":"This dua for grave brings peace and Barakah when placing the deceased, following the Sunnah and asking Allah to make the burial easy and full of mercy for the one in the grave.","lesson":"Bismillah at burial keeps the grave safe with Allah’s name and protection."},{"id":288,"text":"With the Name of Allah and according to the millat of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).","title":"Dua when placing the body in Grave","source":"Sahih. Ibn Majah: 1550","reflection":"This dua for funeral brings comfort and Barakah when placing the body in the grave, following the way of the Messenger of Allah and asking for Allah’s mercy and protection for the deceased.","lesson":"Bismillah at burial gives the grave safety and peace with Allah’s name."},{"id":289,"text":"With the Name of Allah, in the path of Allah and according to the millat of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)","title":"Dua when put the body in Grave","source":"Sahih. Ibn Majah: 1270","reflection":"This dua for the dead brings peace and mercy when placing the body in the grave, following the path of Allah and the Messenger, and asking for Barakah and safety for the deceased.","lesson":"Bismillah at burial gives the grave protection and Allah’s special care."},{"id":290,"text":"Peace be upon you, the inhabitants of the grave, among the believers, and Muslims, and if Allah will then we shall join you. I pray to Allah peace for us and for you.","title":"Dua for Visiting the Grave (Assalamualaikum ya ahlal quboor)","source":"Muslim: 975","reflection":"This dua for visiting the grave brings peace to both the living and those resting, reminding us of our return to Allah and the bond between Muslims even after death.","lesson":"Allah gives Barakah to the one who makes dua for visiting the grave with Iman."},{"id":291,"text":"Peace be upon the inhabitants of this place among the believers and Muslims. May Allah have mercy upon those who have gone on ahead of us and those who come later on, and we will join you, if Allah wills.","title":"Dua for Entering Graveyard (Masnoon Dua)","source":"Sahih. Mishkatul Masabih: 1767","reflection":"This dua for entering graveyard reminds Muslims of the shortness of life, brings mercy for those who passed, and keeps the heart soft with hope in Allah’s forgiveness and kindness.","lesson":"Allah shows Rahmah to Muslims who use this dua for entering graveyard."},{"id":292,"text":"Peace be upon you, O you who believe. We will meet you, if Allah willing.","title":"Dua for Visiting the Grave (Graveyard Dua)","source":"Muslim: 249","reflection":"This dua for visiting the graveyard brings peace to the hearts, connects believers, and reminds us of our own return to Allah, making every visit full of hope and kindness.","lesson":"Allah gives peace to the dead when Muslims say assalamualaikum at graveyard."},{"id":293,"text":"Peace be upon you, O you who believers inhabitants of the grave! The promise that was given to you has come to you, and you are waiting for the day to come. And we will meet you by the will of Allah. O Allah, forgive the inhabitants of the Baqi graveyard.","title":"Dua for Visiting Muslim Graves (Graveyard Dua)","source":"Muslim: 974","reflection":"This dua for graveyard brings hope for forgiveness, connects hearts with those resting, and reminds every Muslim of Allah’s promise and the mercy waiting for all believers.","lesson":"Allah gives maghfirat to the dead when Muslims use this dua for graveyard."}];
